00:32:02,638 --> 00:32:04,998
and moves I haven't done before.

830
00:32:05,198 --> 00:32:07,338
But putting together a part with those moves...

831
00:32:07,438 --> 00:32:08,538
didn't feel right.

832
00:32:09,038 --> 00:32:10,308
That was when I realized this.

833
00:32:10,308 --> 00:32:12,378
"I must be myself to make it feel iconic."

834
00:32:12,478 --> 00:32:14,908
The title of my work is "Becoming."

835
00:32:15,148 --> 00:32:16,718
Where I am right now...

836
00:32:16,848 --> 00:32:19,118
and the process before reaching this far.

837
00:32:19,288 --> 00:32:21,788
I tried to express the emotions...

838
00:32:21,788 --> 00:32:23,158
of the past and present.

839
00:32:23,158 --> 00:32:25,358
I was certain about the emotions.

840
00:32:25,358 --> 00:32:26,828
The screen has to display...

841
00:32:26,828 --> 00:32:29,058
my own feelings...

842
00:32:29,198 --> 00:32:33,528
to be expressed as BABYZOO's iconic energy.

843
00:32:33,528 --> 00:32:34,798
I did a lot of research.

844
00:32:34,798 --> 00:32:36,468
Being true to myself...

845
00:32:36,468 --> 00:32:38,098
was the biggest distinguishing factor.

846
00:32:38,568 --> 00:32:40,708
I think that will be expressed through the video.

847
00:32:40,868 --> 00:32:42,378
We will watch it together.

848
00:32:42,838 --> 00:32:43,878
(Movement Director BABYZOO)

849
00:32:43,878 --> 00:32:44,908
(Synopsis: I'm finally where I wanted to be.)

850
00:32:44,908 --> 00:32:45,908
(Space Utilization Strategy: Unique Energy. Iconic Image)

851
00:32:52,788 --> 00:32:53,788
(Impressed)

852
00:32:53,918 --> 00:32:55,018
Gosh, it was awesome.

853
00:32:55,018 --> 00:32:56,518
Jun Hui filmed a commercial.

854
00:32:57,018 --> 00:32:58,618
Gosh, this feels like a commercial.

855
00:33:01,228 --> 00:33:02,698
"I've made it to this place."

856
00:33:02,728 --> 00:33:05,128
I tried to express that only with my eyes.

857
00:33:05,128 --> 00:33:07,028
Jun Hui has many facial expressions.

858
00:33:07,028 --> 00:33:08,298
I believe that's his strength.

859
00:33:08,398 --> 00:33:09,598
(Mega section)

860
00:33:09,598 --> 00:33:11,168
The nervous and overwhelming emotions...

861
00:33:11,168 --> 00:33:12,738
were expressed through dancing.

862
00:33:12,738 --> 00:33:16,208
I believe it was the best song for BABYZOO to express himself.

863
00:33:16,208 --> 00:33:17,878
(Mega section)

864
00:33:17,878 --> 00:33:21,648
While spinning, I move back to the times I've been through.

865
00:33:21,648 --> 00:33:24,618
Think of me reminiscing about the past.

866
00:33:26,248 --> 00:33:29,358
I did my best to express the intense emotions I felt...

867
00:33:29,358 --> 00:33:32,358
while trying to make it to where I am now.

868
00:33:32,558 --> 00:33:34,788
Every move felt strong.

869
00:33:35,258 --> 00:33:39,068
There were some odd moves that could be seen.

870
00:33:42,068 --> 00:33:43,068
That's great.

871
00:33:43,568 --> 00:33:46,008
Me going through memories of the past. Me in the present.

872
00:33:46,008 --> 00:33:48,768
I expressed the emotions...

873
00:33:48,768 --> 00:33:50,978
of believing that I can move forward again.

874
00:33:51,738 --> 00:33:54,008
I put together a group move.

875
00:33:54,308 --> 00:33:56,078
It seems like I crashed into a wall,

876
00:33:56,078 --> 00:33:57,978
but I get back up from the ground.

877
00:33:57,978 --> 00:34:02,088
(Mega section)

878
00:34:02,818 --> 00:34:04,888
(Clapping...)

879
00:34:04,888 --> 00:34:06,628
(automatically)

880
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:07,688
That was amazing.

881
00:34:08,858 --> 00:34:11,228
Only Jun Hui can pull that off.

882
00:34:11,228 --> 00:34:12,728
Especially, at the start,

883
00:34:12,898 --> 00:34:14,168
there was a move like this.

884
00:34:14,698 --> 00:34:15,998
"It's quite childish."

885
00:34:15,998 --> 00:34:19,138
Jun Hui came up with wow factor with the directing.

886
00:34:19,368 --> 00:34:21,568
But the dancing was quite disappointing.

887
00:34:21,968 --> 00:34:25,138
I was impressed by the clear presentation.

888
00:34:25,508 --> 00:34:29,248
I got a strong impression that this was a brand film.

889
00:34:29,248 --> 00:34:32,148
I was impressed by that. And regardless of this video,

890
00:34:32,148 --> 00:34:34,188
it made me think, "I want to work with this director."

891
00:34:34,188 --> 00:34:36,888
This presentation and video...

892
00:34:37,118 --> 00:34:39,028
made me want to take this project.

893
00:34:39,028 --> 00:34:41,088
I was greatly impressed by...

894
00:34:41,088 --> 00:34:43,558
your directing abilities.

895
00:34:43,798 --> 00:34:47,198
I'm aware that the director in charge of this...

896
00:34:47,198 --> 00:34:48,728
is really busy.

897
00:34:48,728 --> 00:34:50,668
He's really busy,

898
00:34:50,868 --> 00:34:52,638
but it felt like you came up with the actual product...

899
00:34:52,638 --> 00:34:55,308
that could be used right away.

900
00:34:55,308 --> 00:34:57,578
I thought that it was directed in detail...

901
00:34:57,578 --> 00:35:00,378
and that the director in charge would find it easy to work with.

902
00:35:00,378 --> 00:35:02,918
It starts with the whole group at the start.

903
00:35:02,918 --> 00:35:04,218
You looked into the camera...

904
00:35:04,218 --> 00:35:07,788
before the group joins in. That part felt different...

905
00:35:07,848 --> 00:35:09,488
and I thought it was a good idea.

906
00:35:09,488 --> 00:35:11,258
As he just mentioned,

907
00:35:11,388 --> 00:35:13,328
it seems like I won't have to do much with this.

908
00:35:14,258 --> 00:35:16,998
You've done a great job in a short period of time.

909
00:35:17,128 --> 00:35:21,168
I could've made it stronger and more impactful,

910
00:35:21,168 --> 00:35:24,238
but I believed that a sense of control and empty space...

911
00:35:24,238 --> 00:35:26,168
suited the brand more.

912
00:35:26,238 --> 00:35:29,838
That was why I made a bold choice to empty out some parts.

913
00:35:30,038 --> 00:35:31,978
I have no regrets about what I came up with.

914
00:35:32,978 --> 00:35:35,078
I believe I'm someone...

915
00:35:35,078 --> 00:35:37,018
who has a great sense of expression in films.

916
00:35:37,018 --> 00:35:39,118
I'm really confident and I'm able to say this.

917
00:35:39,288 --> 00:35:40,518
You must pick me.

918
00:35:41,718 --> 00:35:43,318
Hello, I'm Choreographer Back Koo Young.

919
00:35:43,318 --> 00:35:44,588
(Back Koo Young is the last one to go.)

920
00:35:44,688 --> 00:35:47,458
Koo Young has a great understanding of videos.

921
00:35:47,458 --> 00:35:48,828
He's always a concern.

922
00:35:48,928 --> 00:35:51,258
I'm excited to see how impressive his work is.

923
00:35:51,398 --> 00:35:53,298
After he heard about the mission,

924
00:35:53,298 --> 00:35:55,528
his ambition poured out from his eyes.

925
00:35:55,528 --> 00:35:57,368
The mission was about taking the spotlight.

926
00:35:57,368 --> 00:35:58,468
I really wanted to take this role.

927
00:35:58,468 --> 00:36:01,108
"SUPERNOVA" is my concept.

928
00:36:01,268 --> 00:36:03,178
"One spark, infinite energy."

929
00:36:03,178 --> 00:36:04,438
My inspiration...

930
00:36:04,438 --> 00:36:06,308
came from "Explosion of a Star."

931
00:36:06,308 --> 00:36:08,548
A star explodes...

932
00:36:08,548 --> 00:36:10,248
and the stars around explode due to that energy.

933
00:36:10,248 --> 00:36:12,248
I did my best to express that idea.

934
00:36:12,718 --> 00:36:15,418
A small burst of energy expands into a great burst of energy.

935
00:36:15,418 --> 00:36:16,418
(Impressed)

936
00:36:16,418 --> 00:36:19,058
He even brought an image made by AI.

937
00:36:19,158 --> 00:36:20,358
"He secured the Title Sequence Film."

938
00:36:20,358 --> 00:36:21,688
"He's planning to secure this one as well."

939
00:36:21,688 --> 00:36:23,398
"He's up for this." These were the thoughts I got.

940
00:36:23,458 --> 00:36:25,258
I prepared everything with great care.

941
00:36:25,258 --> 00:36:27,398
The highlight in the film...

942
00:36:27,398 --> 00:36:28,568
is the 360° section.

943
00:36:29,298 --> 00:36:30,798
From here to here.

944
00:36:30,968 --> 00:36:33,108
I set the angles based on the movements.

945
00:36:33,308 --> 00:36:34,508
(A 360° turn)

946
00:36:34,508 --> 00:36:35,508
(The camera turns as well.)

947
00:36:35,608 --> 00:36:37,478
I did this dozens of times...

948
00:36:37,478 --> 00:36:38,878
until I got the right cut.

949
00:36:39,248 --> 00:36:40,378
There we go.

950
00:36:40,648 --> 00:36:42,108
While changing conception of the wall and floor,

951
00:36:42,108 --> 00:36:43,448
I wanted to defy gravity...

952
00:36:43,448 --> 00:36:44,618
and express an image...

953
00:36:44,618 --> 00:36:46,718
of penetrating through a limited area.

954
00:36:46,888 --> 00:36:49,558
Once that energy exceeds the limit of that area,

955
00:36:49,558 --> 00:36:51,818
one spark becomes infinite energy.

956
00:36:51,818 --> 00:36:55,698
In the video, the solo dancer would turn into the mega crew.

957
00:36:55,698 --> 00:36:57,498
Koo Young did well with the presentation.

958
00:36:57,498 --> 00:36:59,198
I'm curious about what he came up with.

959
00:36:59,198 --> 00:37:01,668
I was confident in the result that came out.

960
00:37:01,668 --> 00:37:04,438
I will make sure to take the title as Movement Director.

961
00:37:04,438 --> 00:37:05,538
(Movement Director Back Koo Young)

962
00:37:05,538 --> 00:37:06,738
(Synopsis: One ray of light reaches an unfamiliar place.)

963
00:37:06,738 --> 00:37:07,908
(Space Utilization Strategy: Trapped energy exceeds limit)

964
00:37:07,908 --> 00:37:08,938
(Brand Performance Film Mission, Choreography Concept Credit Board)

965
00:37:08,938 --> 00:37:10,038
(Back Koo Young)

966
00:37:16,448 --> 00:37:17,978
(Impressed)

967
00:37:17,978 --> 00:37:19,348
(Solo section)

968
00:37:19,348 --> 00:37:21,248
It started strong.

969
00:37:21,988 --> 00:37:24,058
I wanted to add life to the film...

970
00:37:24,058 --> 00:37:26,458
using angles and transitions.

971
00:37:26,888 --> 00:37:27,958
It was really impressive.

972
00:37:28,028 --> 00:37:29,728
As the angles were unique,

973
00:37:29,728 --> 00:37:31,958
it felt iconic.

974
00:37:32,098 --> 00:37:34,598
As it was a limited space,

975
00:37:34,598 --> 00:37:37,068
I wanted to express a distorted and crumpling image.

976
00:37:37,068 --> 00:37:39,538
(Solo section)

977
00:37:39,538 --> 00:37:41,608
I wish the viewers to find it entertaining.

978
00:37:41,838 --> 00:37:42,908
It was really charming.

979
00:37:42,908 --> 00:37:45,108
He didn't make a name for himself for no reason.

980
00:37:45,108 --> 00:37:49,948
(Solo section)

981
00:37:49,948 --> 00:37:53,188
It didn't feel like he was defying gravity.

982
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:57,858
(Solo section)

983
00:37:57,858 --> 00:38:00,558
I used the jump for an expansion of the area...

984
00:38:00,558 --> 00:38:03,198
to start the mega performance.

985
00:38:03,528 --> 00:38:06,998
As the camera turns, I head back to the solo section.

986
00:38:07,098 --> 00:38:10,898
I didn't understand why it went back to the solo section.

987
00:38:11,368 --> 00:38:13,838
I do another jump to connect to the mega performance.

988
00:38:13,838 --> 00:38:15,108
(Mega section)

989
00:38:15,108 --> 00:38:17,578
The tension and energy were amazing.

990
00:38:17,578 --> 00:38:20,148
(Mega section)

991
00:38:22,208 --> 00:38:23,218
(Impressed on mute)

992
00:38:24,448 --> 00:38:27,418
It was a lot more impressive than I expected it to be.

993
00:38:27,418 --> 00:38:29,618
The structure and flow of the performance were impressive.

994
00:38:29,618 --> 00:38:32,988
Koo Young showed that he could be impactful as a player as well.

995
00:38:33,228 --> 00:38:34,788
Compared to the concept,

996
00:38:34,788 --> 00:38:37,558
the dancing and expressions felt too aggressive.

997
00:38:37,558 --> 00:38:41,668
It started with strong energy and ended with strong energy.

998
00:38:41,668 --> 00:38:43,568
I think my body will break from that.

999
00:38:43,638 --> 00:38:44,738
I won't be able to do that.

1000
00:38:44,898 --> 00:38:46,668
It would be great if the Judges...

1001
00:38:46,668 --> 00:38:49,638
would find this to be the right film for the final chapter.

1002
00:38:49,738 --> 00:38:52,108
Your directing abilities...

1003
00:38:52,108 --> 00:38:54,978
and dancing abilities stood out in this video.

1004
00:38:54,978 --> 00:38:56,178
I was very impressed.

1005
00:38:56,618 --> 00:38:58,578
This is what I'm curious about.

1006
00:38:58,578 --> 00:39:01,948
The concept is "SUPERNOVA: One spark, infinite energy."

1007
00:39:01,948 --> 00:39:04,888
When will that transition of an explosion to infinite energy...

1008
00:39:04,888 --> 00:39:06,228
actually happen?

1009
00:39:06,428 --> 00:39:08,858
The lights change during the jump.

1010
00:39:08,858 --> 00:39:10,198
This was the image I had in my head.

1011
00:39:10,198 --> 00:39:13,368
As I jump, the mega crew jumps.

1012
00:39:13,368 --> 00:39:15,098
I thought it could be expressed through post-production.

1013
00:39:15,728 --> 00:39:17,538
So the director...

1014
00:39:17,538 --> 00:39:19,268
will come up with the scene for the explosion?

1015
00:39:20,168 --> 00:39:21,768
(Will it not be possible?)

1016
00:39:21,768 --> 00:39:24,078
I thought that it was different.

1017
00:39:24,078 --> 00:39:26,578
It was completely different from what I expected.

1018
00:39:27,208 --> 00:39:28,578
(Flustered)

1019
00:39:28,808 --> 00:39:30,178
He must not like it.

1020
00:39:30,578 --> 00:39:33,048
But it had a strong impact.

1021
00:39:33,048 --> 00:39:36,358
I thought that the way you expressed gravity...

1022
00:39:36,358 --> 00:39:38,418
would be really impactful in the master film.

1023
00:39:38,418 --> 00:39:40,428
But this is what I'm worried about.

1024
00:39:40,428 --> 00:39:42,998
The members of the mega crew have to dance as one.

1025
00:39:42,998 --> 00:39:46,328
I have a slight worry about whether that could be expressed perfectly.

1026
00:39:46,328 --> 00:39:47,568
If it doesn't work out on site,

1027
00:39:47,568 --> 00:39:49,538
everyone will look glum.

1028
00:39:50,998 --> 00:39:55,368
He was worried about making the mega crew performance.

1029
00:39:55,368 --> 00:39:57,038
It's not a matter of whether it's possible or not.

1030
00:39:57,038 --> 00:39:58,138
It's something that must happen.

1031
00:39:58,138 --> 00:40:01,148
You won't have to worry about that.

1032
00:40:01,148 --> 00:40:03,878
I will do my best to come up with a good performance.

1033
00:40:04,018 --> 00:40:05,448
It's all or nothing.

1034
00:40:05,448 --> 00:40:07,318
He said it was different from what he expected.

1035
00:40:07,318 --> 00:40:09,688
It could be positive or negative.

1036
00:40:09,958 --> 00:40:11,758
I hoped to get the role.

1037
00:40:11,758 --> 00:40:13,588
I thought that I was the one who came up with...

1038
00:40:13,588 --> 00:40:15,898
the best video with energy.

1039
00:40:15,898 --> 00:40:17,658
I'm desperate for this.

1040
00:40:17,658 --> 00:40:19,598
I'm the most desperate for this one out of all missions.

1041
00:40:19,598 --> 00:40:20,798
Please pick me.

1042
00:40:20,928 --> 00:40:23,338
That concludes the check of the solo performance films...

1043
00:40:23,338 --> 00:40:26,908
of all five choreographers.

1044
00:40:26,908 --> 00:40:30,538
To decide on just one director who will become...

1045
00:40:30,538 --> 00:40:33,048
the movement director of the Brand Performance Film,

1046
00:40:33,048 --> 00:40:35,948
we will have our final discussion.

1047
00:40:36,248 --> 00:40:39,548
Please head to your Directors' Room...

1048
00:40:39,548 --> 00:40:42,188
and wait for the final result.

1049
00:40:42,188 --> 00:40:43,488
(Scared)

1050
00:40:43,488 --> 00:40:45,158
Let's leave it to my fate.

1051
00:40:46,028 --> 00:40:47,128
- Let's leave it to my fate. - Thank you!

1052
00:40:47,128 --> 00:40:48,488
- Thank you! - Thank you!

1053
00:40:48,488 --> 00:40:49,928
- Thank you! - Thank you!

1054
00:40:49,928 --> 00:40:50,928
(Smiling)

1055
00:40:51,128 --> 00:40:52,428
You did a great job.

1056
00:40:52,428 --> 00:40:53,898
I did my best.

1057
00:40:53,898 --> 00:40:55,598
I have no regrets.

1058
00:40:56,838 --> 00:40:58,368
They're deciding there?

1059
00:40:58,398 --> 00:41:00,038
Gosh, this is crazy.

1060
00:41:00,038 --> 00:41:01,668
Can't they do it in a separate room?

1061
00:41:01,668 --> 00:41:04,078
Through all of the synopses...

1062
00:41:04,078 --> 00:41:06,248
and presentations,

1063
00:41:06,248 --> 00:41:07,878
I believe mine stood out...

1064
00:41:09,448 --> 00:41:10,948
out of all of them.

1065
00:41:10,948 --> 00:41:12,478
If I become the movement director,

1066
00:41:12,478 --> 00:41:15,048
I get the right to save one person.

1067
00:41:15,048 --> 00:41:16,388
I'm desperate.

1068
00:41:16,388 --> 00:41:17,558
Gosh, I'm so curious.

1069
00:41:17,558 --> 00:41:18,788
I'm so curious about what's going on at this moment.

1070
00:41:18,788 --> 00:41:20,858
It's a bummer that I can't hear anything.

1071
00:41:20,858 --> 00:41:22,058
I think mine will feel more impactful...

1072
00:41:22,058 --> 00:41:23,328
when they watch it over.

1073
00:41:23,328 --> 00:41:24,958
Please go with my idea.

1074
00:41:24,958 --> 00:41:27,898
If my idea meets with the director's idea,

1075
00:41:27,898 --> 00:41:30,168
I believe a great video will come to life.

1076
00:41:30,798 --> 00:41:32,368
I really want to do this.

1077
00:41:32,368 --> 00:41:33,938
Everyone would feel that way.

1078
00:41:33,938 --> 00:41:35,268
Everyone wants this role.

1079
00:41:35,508 --> 00:41:36,878
I hope mine gets picked.

1080
00:41:37,208 --> 00:41:39,508
The directors are in a heated discussion.

1081
00:41:39,978 --> 00:41:41,708
Do you have the ranks in your head?

1082
00:41:41,708 --> 00:41:43,118
I do, but they all have...

1083
00:41:43,118 --> 00:41:45,348
- different strengths. - Right.

1084
00:41:45,348 --> 00:41:46,818
We are in need of two things.

1085
00:41:46,818 --> 00:41:47,848
We need a model...

1086
00:41:47,848 --> 00:41:49,318
and directing abilities.

1087
00:41:49,318 --> 00:41:51,488
This is the hardest part for me.

1088
00:41:51,488 --> 00:41:54,058
I asked them to express an iconic performance.

1089
00:41:54,228 --> 00:41:55,888
When you come up with the solo performance,

1090
00:41:55,888 --> 00:41:58,728
you might have to consider a group dance as well.

1091
00:41:58,728 --> 00:42:01,498
It would be great to have ideas on the transition to the solo part...

1092
00:42:01,498 --> 00:42:07,568
and how to make an impact with your appearance.

1093
00:42:07,568 --> 00:42:10,108
They all interpreted it differently.

1094
00:42:10,108 --> 00:42:12,538
As for INGYOO,

1095
00:42:12,538 --> 00:42:15,978
