1238
00:47:53,588 --> 00:47:55,248
Based on that thought,

1239
00:47:55,248 --> 00:47:58,118
I think I would lean toward BADA and BABYZOO.

1240
00:47:58,118 --> 00:48:00,788
- They're my top two as well. - Right.

1241
00:48:00,788 --> 00:48:02,558
I'm thinking the same way.

1242
00:48:02,888 --> 00:48:04,328
Who will it be?

1243
00:48:04,528 --> 00:48:05,598
BABYZOO.

1244
00:48:05,598 --> 00:48:06,828
(Answering his own question)

1245
00:48:07,128 --> 00:48:09,028
I hope I get picked.

1246
00:48:09,028 --> 00:48:11,338
I will avoid the Last Stage and head to the final.

1247
00:48:11,338 --> 00:48:13,138
I don't want to go to the Last Stage. It can't happen.

1248
00:48:13,138 --> 00:48:14,568
Never.

1249
00:48:14,568 --> 00:48:16,808
"I'm done if it doesn't work out for me this time."

1250
00:48:16,808 --> 00:48:19,038
"It's game over for me if I fail this time."

1251
00:48:19,038 --> 00:48:22,108
I kept believing that I was going to get picked.

1252
00:48:23,248 --> 00:48:24,478
Iconic.

1253
00:48:24,478 --> 00:48:26,888
I'm a true icon.

1254
00:48:28,388 --> 00:48:31,758
But it's based on the draft.

1255
00:48:31,858 --> 00:48:33,628
Dance like INGYOO when you have a lot in mind.

1256
00:48:34,288 --> 00:48:37,498
I've always wanted to put together a smartphone commercial.

1257
00:48:37,498 --> 00:48:39,228
It was a personal dream.

1258
00:48:39,228 --> 00:48:40,998
I want it so much.

1259
00:48:40,998 --> 00:48:43,638
I really want to be picked as the movement director.

1260
00:48:43,638 --> 00:48:46,938
(Who will become the movement director?)

1261
00:48:47,168 --> 00:48:49,008
BADA is so iconic.

1262
00:48:49,108 --> 00:48:51,938
She must've been really compelling as the subject.

1263
00:48:51,938 --> 00:48:53,978
BABYZOO was the most prepared.

1264
00:48:54,248 --> 00:48:55,878
And his direction had a real hook.

1265
00:48:56,148 --> 00:48:59,178
(Who will become Movement Director?)

1266
00:49:02,048 --> 00:49:05,558
(Final Movement Director: BABYZOO)

1267
00:49:06,888 --> 00:49:07,888
(Really? Me?)

1268
00:49:07,888 --> 00:49:08,888
What?

1269
00:49:09,028 --> 00:49:10,858
Then the screen turned orange.

1270
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:12,498
(It's really me!)

1271
00:49:12,498 --> 00:49:13,828
I totally froze...

1272
00:49:13,928 --> 00:49:16,298
Was it really me? That's crazy.

1273
00:49:16,538 --> 00:49:18,598
Yes!

1274
00:49:18,898 --> 00:49:20,168
I was so happy.

1275
00:49:20,268 --> 00:49:21,738
(Good job, me!)

1276
00:49:21,738 --> 00:49:24,178
I finally did something on Street World Fighter.

1277
00:49:24,178 --> 00:49:26,478
I didn't want to seem overrated again,

1278
00:49:26,478 --> 00:49:28,678
so I knew I had to prepare even harder and nail the shoot.

1279
00:49:28,678 --> 00:49:29,878
That's what hit me right away.

1280
00:49:31,248 --> 00:49:32,248
What?

1281
00:49:33,118 --> 00:49:34,588
Congrats.

1282
00:49:34,748 --> 00:49:36,218
I was really disappointed.

1283
00:49:36,218 --> 00:49:38,318
It was something I'd really looked forward to,

1284
00:49:38,458 --> 00:49:39,958
but in that draft video,

1285
00:49:40,328 --> 00:49:42,528
I don't think I explained it well enough.

1286
00:49:42,528 --> 00:49:43,928
Yes, I was pretty disappointed.

1287
00:49:44,228 --> 00:49:47,068
BABYZOO checked all six boxes in this mission.

1288
00:49:47,268 --> 00:49:49,368
He said I only checked five.

1289
00:49:49,768 --> 00:49:50,998
(During BADA's presentation)

1290
00:49:51,198 --> 00:49:53,208
(Not many people check all six boxes)

1291
00:49:53,508 --> 00:49:55,508
(Five-out-of-six BADA wraps up)

1292
00:49:56,168 --> 00:49:58,308
(BABYZOO's presentation follows)

1293
00:49:58,308 --> 00:50:00,648
(I take back what I said about no one checking all six boxes.)

1294
00:50:00,848 --> 00:50:03,278
(Disappointed, happy)

1295
00:50:03,418 --> 00:50:05,078
From what I saw...

1296
00:50:05,078 --> 00:50:07,488
- I thought it was totally over. - Right.

1297
00:50:07,488 --> 00:50:08,548
The direction was so good.

1298
00:50:08,548 --> 00:50:10,018
That opening close-up...

1299
00:50:10,018 --> 00:50:12,758
The look in his eyes, the mood. It all had such a strong impact.

1300
00:50:12,758 --> 00:50:15,188
It's the only one that really focuses on the subject.

1301
00:50:15,188 --> 00:50:16,658
That works so well as an ending.

1302
00:50:16,658 --> 00:50:17,828
Right. It's so good.

1303
00:50:17,828 --> 00:50:19,498
If they shoot it just like that,

1304
00:50:19,498 --> 00:50:21,228
- you can relax a little. - Definitely.

1305
00:50:21,228 --> 00:50:22,398
It's like having the answer key.

1306
00:50:22,398 --> 00:50:24,538
Everything's all figured out now.

1307
00:50:25,498 --> 00:50:26,638
Is BABYZOO crying?

1308
00:50:26,738 --> 00:50:29,138
My eyes actually started tearing up.

1309
00:50:29,408 --> 00:50:30,938
It was such an overwhelming feeling.

1310
00:50:31,378 --> 00:50:33,748
I can't believe my moment finally came.

1311
00:50:33,848 --> 00:50:35,448
As the missions went on,

1312
00:50:35,448 --> 00:50:37,678
I kept wondering if I'd make it all the way to the finals,

1313
00:50:38,248 --> 00:50:40,248
and I started to worry.

1314
00:50:41,018 --> 00:50:43,788
I kept questioning whether I had what it takes as a director.

1315
00:50:43,788 --> 00:50:46,188
And there were so many times I really doubted myself.

1316
00:50:46,188 --> 00:50:49,788
I thought I might not even get to show what I can do in the finals.

1317
00:50:50,228 --> 00:50:51,298
So I... I made the finals?

1318
00:50:52,458 --> 00:50:53,998
I can't believe I'm in the finals.

1319
00:50:54,268 --> 00:50:56,598
The best part is making the finals.

1320
00:50:56,598 --> 00:50:57,938
Now I get to go straight there...

1321
00:50:58,038 --> 00:50:59,698
so I'll take more responsibility...

1322
00:50:59,698 --> 00:51:02,538
and put even more heart into it.

1323
00:51:02,808 --> 00:51:03,908
Jun Hui!

1324
00:51:05,208 --> 00:51:06,948
I'm disappointed, but I am happy for Jun Hui.

1325
00:51:06,948 --> 00:51:08,508
I genuinely think he's amazing.

1326
00:51:08,508 --> 00:51:10,918
Kasper is genuinely rooting for me.

1327
00:51:10,918 --> 00:51:13,648
I'm genuinely so happy that Jun Hui became the director.

1328
00:51:13,988 --> 00:51:16,048
BABYZOO, let's get it!

1329
00:51:16,388 --> 00:51:19,118
Right now, I think the most disappointed person is...

1330
00:51:19,858 --> 00:51:20,858
Back Koo Young.

1331
00:51:21,188 --> 00:51:22,358
Jun Hui pulled it off.

1332
00:51:23,358 --> 00:51:24,728
Oh, Last Stage. Darn it.

1333
00:51:25,558 --> 00:51:26,928
Jun Hui, please save me.

1334
00:51:27,198 --> 00:51:30,838
I've been given the power to save one person.

1335
00:51:30,938 --> 00:51:32,438
(The clear-eyed madman)

1336
00:51:32,438 --> 00:51:34,308
Does he want to go to Last Stage?

1337
00:51:34,868 --> 00:51:36,978
I think it's about time...

1338
00:51:36,978 --> 00:51:38,778
I get to tease him for once.

1339
00:51:38,778 --> 00:51:40,148
He would never save me.

1340
00:51:40,478 --> 00:51:42,948
This is the first time I've felt this disappointed.

1341
00:51:42,948 --> 00:51:46,248
I'd been on a winning streak,

1342
00:51:46,348 --> 00:51:49,348
so I felt really down this time.

1343
00:51:49,448 --> 00:51:52,288
I hope Jun Hui saves me. Please.

1344
00:51:52,388 --> 00:51:54,828
Now I need to do all I can to get saved.

1345
00:51:56,128 --> 00:51:57,628
(The sweet taste of power)

1346
00:51:57,628 --> 00:52:00,098
(Endless applause)

1347
00:52:00,098 --> 00:52:03,228
In the brand performance film, the four choreographers...

1348
00:52:03,338 --> 00:52:04,538
will each be assigned one part...

1349
00:52:04,538 --> 00:52:07,908
and serve as its movement director.

1350
00:52:08,108 --> 00:52:09,508
(Part Movement Directing)

1351
00:52:09,508 --> 00:52:10,608
I thought so.

1352
00:52:10,608 --> 00:52:12,708
In tight spaces, tubes and such.

1353
00:52:12,708 --> 00:52:14,108
BABYZOO...

1354
00:52:14,208 --> 00:52:17,478
will review the movement direction for each person's part...

1355
00:52:17,478 --> 00:52:20,888
then choose just one person to save.

1356
00:52:20,888 --> 00:52:24,318
I know Last Stage is a very scary place,

1357
00:52:24,318 --> 00:52:26,258
so Koo Young definitely has to go.

1358
00:52:26,258 --> 00:52:27,488
I hope BABYZOO sends him there.

1359
00:52:27,488 --> 00:52:30,498
Jun Hui is choosing someone to join him in the finals.

1360
00:52:30,498 --> 00:52:32,258
Please pick me.

1361
00:52:32,398 --> 00:52:33,898
There's one important condition.

1362
00:52:34,168 --> 00:52:35,798
In the part you direct,

1363
00:52:35,798 --> 00:52:38,838
you cannot take part as a dancer.

1364
00:52:38,838 --> 00:52:39,968
(Part Movement Directing: They must direct one another.)

1365
00:52:39,968 --> 00:52:41,538
We take turns directing each other?

1366
00:52:41,538 --> 00:52:43,708
They've come up with another interesting rule.

1367
00:52:43,708 --> 00:52:47,508
We're creating parts just for the directors,

1368
00:52:47,508 --> 00:52:48,848
so I thought I'd have to study up quite a bit.

1369
00:52:48,848 --> 00:52:51,778
I've already figured out what everyone here is like.

1370
00:52:51,778 --> 00:52:53,688
We have great dancers to work with.

1371
00:52:53,688 --> 00:52:55,218
When you have great dancers,

1372
00:52:55,218 --> 00:52:56,688
it makes a difference in the result.

1373
00:52:57,118 --> 00:52:59,188
Together with BABYZOO, our movement director,

1374
00:52:59,188 --> 00:53:02,188
we chose the director and dancer for each part.

1375
00:53:02,188 --> 00:53:04,558
We'll now reveal each part's movement director.

1376
00:53:05,398 --> 00:53:08,228
(Part 1: Music and storyboard reveal)

1377
00:53:08,668 --> 00:53:12,098
For this part, we've built a curved hallway.

1378
00:53:12,098 --> 00:53:14,838
The choreographer will be hidden, then suddenly come into view.

1379
00:53:14,838 --> 00:53:17,938
I think this part plays on the fun of having a curved hallway.

1380
00:53:17,938 --> 00:53:19,338
The director for Part 1 is...

1381
00:53:19,338 --> 00:53:21,808
I think I can do a good job with that curved hallway.

1382
00:53:21,908 --> 00:53:25,048
I think the focus will be on making the performer stand out.

1383
00:53:25,318 --> 00:53:27,748
It looks hard. It could be fun.

1384
00:53:27,748 --> 00:53:28,748
I was torn between the two.

1385
00:53:28,748 --> 00:53:30,958
What you can express on a curve...

1386
00:53:30,958 --> 00:53:33,088
seems limited to me.

1387
00:53:33,288 --> 00:53:35,558
Part One's director is INGYOO.

1388
00:53:35,558 --> 00:53:36,558
(Part 1 movement director: INGYOO)

1389
00:53:37,058 --> 00:53:38,058
(Part 1 movement director: INGYOO)

1390
00:53:39,928 --> 00:53:43,198
The director dancing in Part 1 is...

1391
00:53:43,198 --> 00:53:45,098
I do want to direct BADA.

1392
00:53:45,098 --> 00:53:47,808
She's the best performer here.

1393
00:53:47,908 --> 00:53:51,178
The director taking part as a dancer is BADA.

1394
00:53:51,778 --> 00:53:53,208
(Part 1 dancer: BADA)

1395
00:53:53,208 --> 00:53:54,208
(Part 1 movement director: INGYOO)

1396
00:53:54,208 --> 00:53:55,208
Yes!

1397
00:53:55,208 --> 00:53:56,248
(Part 1 dancer: BADA, movement director: INGYOO)

1398
00:53:56,248 --> 00:53:57,448
The best performer!

1399
00:53:58,078 --> 00:54:00,888
"Wouldn't BADA want me to direct her?"

1400
00:54:00,888 --> 00:54:02,118
That moment has finally come.

1401
00:54:02,118 --> 00:54:06,118
Will INGYOO be able to use my skills to the fullest?

1402
00:54:06,258 --> 00:54:08,088
I'll do my best. I have an idea.

1403
00:54:08,328 --> 00:54:10,128
This part is in a narrow hallway.

1404
00:54:10,128 --> 00:54:12,058
The dancers go from a jumble to an orderly formation,

1405
00:54:12,058 --> 00:54:14,298
as we move between those at the back and those at the front.

1406
00:54:14,298 --> 00:54:16,028
That's the concept for this part.

1407
00:54:16,228 --> 00:54:17,538
From order to disorder.

1408
00:54:17,538 --> 00:54:19,368
That kind of feel would be so cool.

1409
00:54:19,368 --> 00:54:20,708
(Who should it be?)

1410
00:54:21,168 --> 00:54:24,208
Part Two's movement director is Back Koo Young.

1411
00:54:24,208 --> 00:54:25,208
(Part 2 movement director: Back Koo Young)

1412
00:54:25,208 --> 00:54:26,678
(Part 2 movement director: Back Koo Young)

1413
00:54:27,148 --> 00:54:28,308
I am a little worried.

1414
00:54:28,608 --> 00:54:30,818
It's a really narrow hallway.

1415
00:54:30,818 --> 00:54:33,218
Until we get to the set,

1416
00:54:33,218 --> 00:54:34,988
we have to rehearse just imagining the space.

1417
00:54:34,988 --> 00:54:36,388
Will it work? Will it be okay?

1418
00:54:36,388 --> 00:54:37,918
(Oh, this isn't easy.)

1419
00:54:37,918 --> 00:54:39,358
The dancer for Part Two is...

1420
00:54:39,988 --> 00:54:43,428
I feel like INGYOO won't come well prepared,

1421
00:54:43,828 --> 00:54:46,498
and BADA is INGYOO's dancer.

1422
00:54:46,498 --> 00:54:47,898
Tae Woo seems perfect for it.

1423
00:54:47,898 --> 00:54:51,238
The director dancing in Part Two is Kasper.

1424
00:54:51,568 --> 00:54:53,638
Good. That's great!

1425
00:54:53,638 --> 00:54:54,808
Kim Tae Woo as the dancer?

1426
00:54:54,808 --> 00:54:57,308
His arms are fast. They're long, but fast.

1427
00:54:57,308 --> 00:54:58,708
You know Kasper's go-to move.

1428
00:54:58,708 --> 00:54:59,978
(Kasper's signature: fast moves with long arms)

1429
00:54:59,978 --> 00:55:03,648
I should come up with ways to make Kasper stand out.

1430
00:55:03,848 --> 00:55:05,448
Let's reveal the next part.

1431
00:55:06,118 --> 00:55:08,688
The choreography takes place inside a room,

1432
00:55:08,788 --> 00:55:10,718
and that space will keep repeating.

1433
00:55:10,718 --> 00:55:12,558
We show the same room over and over again,

1434
00:55:12,558 --> 00:55:14,488
but keep changing the choreography. I think that would be fun.

1435
00:55:14,588 --> 00:55:16,288
The camera moves sideways like this.

1436
00:55:16,288 --> 00:55:18,798
- People dance in each room. - Room, room, room.

1437
00:55:18,898 --> 00:55:20,898
I like this part.

1438
00:55:20,998 --> 00:55:24,468
The director for Showcase Three is BADA.

1439
00:55:24,468 --> 00:55:26,738
(Part 3 movement director: BADA)

1440
00:55:26,908 --> 00:55:30,108
The director dancing in Part Three is INGYOO.

1441
00:55:30,208 --> 00:55:32,408
Yes! Very good.

1442
00:55:32,408 --> 00:55:34,648
INGYOO is...

1443
00:55:34,648 --> 00:55:37,518
so good at moving freely,

1444
00:55:37,518 --> 00:55:38,778
so I thought he'd be a good dancer.

1445
00:55:39,048 --> 00:55:40,948
BADA dances for INGYOO,

1446
00:55:40,948 --> 00:55:43,048
and INGYOO dances for BADA.

1447
00:55:43,048 --> 00:55:45,588
The exact matchup from the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

1448
00:55:45,588 --> 00:55:48,358
When INGYOO dances,

1449
00:55:48,458 --> 00:55:49,528
he's fearless

1450
00:55:49,528 --> 00:55:52,928
With INGYOO's unique mood and vibe,

1451
00:55:52,928 --> 00:55:54,798
if I can just capture them on film,

1452
00:55:54,798 --> 00:55:56,898
I think I've got a good shot.

1453
00:55:57,298 --> 00:55:58,968
We'll reveal the next part.

1454
00:56:00,268 --> 00:56:04,638
When you start the choreography, it looks like it goes on forever.

1455
00:56:04,878 --> 00:56:07,308
Your movements and body lines...

1456
00:56:07,308 --> 00:56:09,278
all line up at once, like a fractal,

1457
00:56:09,378 --> 00:56:12,648
so this part should have quite a visual impact.

1458
00:56:14,748 --> 00:56:16,588
Did BABYZOO have me in mind?

1459
00:56:16,588 --> 00:56:19,588
I think he gave me a relatively easy part.

1460
00:56:19,888 --> 00:56:22,828
Even this move will keep repeating.

1461
00:56:22,828 --> 00:56:24,258
There's only one person left,

1462
00:56:24,358 --> 00:56:27,868
but the director for Showcase Four is Kasper.

1463
00:56:27,868 --> 00:56:29,168
(Part 4 movement director: Kasper)

1464
00:56:29,428 --> 00:56:30,968
(Part 4 movement director: Kasper)

1465
00:56:30,968 --> 00:56:35,508
Koo Young would be ideal as the dancer...

1466
00:56:35,508 --> 00:56:37,238
That's what we discussed.

1467
00:56:38,038 --> 00:56:39,678
I'm fine with whoever it is.

1468
00:56:39,678 --> 00:56:42,278
Koo Young has long arms for his height.

1469
00:56:42,278 --> 00:56:43,678
He really extends his arms.

1470
00:56:44,418 --> 00:56:46,748
(Part movement directors and dancers paired up)

1471
00:56:46,748 --> 00:56:49,848
They're judging scene direction, not the dancing, right?

1472
00:56:49,848 --> 00:56:51,288
The best director gets saved?

1473
00:56:51,288 --> 00:56:52,288
Yes.

1474
00:56:53,018 --> 00:56:54,758
You have to work like crazy. Got it?

1475
00:56:55,058 --> 00:56:56,358
(That goes for you too.)

1476
00:56:56,528 --> 00:56:58,328
- INGYOO will get saved. - Why?

1477
00:56:58,328 --> 00:56:59,958
Because BADA is his dancer?

1478
00:57:00,158 --> 00:57:01,528
(Last Stage: 24H)

1479
00:57:01,528 --> 00:57:02,928
(Last Stage: 24H, a final battle to avoid elimination)

1480
00:57:02,928 --> 00:57:04,338
(Available exclusively on TVING)

1481
00:57:05,368 --> 00:57:07,008
(Movement Cross Directing rehearsals begin.)

1482
00:57:07,168 --> 00:57:08,608
Thank you.

1483
00:57:09,138 --> 00:57:10,378
My part involved...

1484
00:57:10,378 --> 00:57:14,048
INGYOO doing movements inside a small room.

1485
00:57:14,048 --> 00:57:15,878
Since other dancers were involved,

1486
00:57:15,878 --> 00:57:18,518
even with the others dancing hard,

1487
00:57:18,518 --> 00:57:19,678
I had to keep the focus on INGYOO.

1488
00:57:19,678 --> 00:57:22,718
In a way, I had a tough part to direct.

1489
00:57:22,718 --> 00:57:25,488
I taped out the space on the floor to get a feel for it.

1490
00:57:25,488 --> 00:57:28,128
I wondered how she'd direct me.

1491
00:57:28,388 --> 00:57:31,558
I hoped she'd direct me in a way that brought out my best.

1492
00:57:31,558 --> 00:57:32,598
That's what I was thinking.

1493
00:57:32,598 --> 00:57:33,968
INGYOO, shouldn't you do this here?

1494
00:57:33,968 --> 00:57:34,998
What?

1495
00:57:34,998 --> 00:57:35,998
(That's the spirit!)

1496
00:57:35,998 --> 00:57:37,138
We can't leave that out.

1497
00:57:37,268 --> 00:57:39,798
INGYOO wanted to find his own soul.

1498
00:57:39,968 --> 00:57:43,738
I wanted his movements to convey that soul,

1499
00:57:43,738 --> 00:57:45,578
so I studied INGYOO a lot.

1500
00:57:45,678 --> 00:57:47,308
I scrolled through his entire Instagram feed...

1501
00:57:47,308 --> 00:57:49,008
to see what kinds of moves he likes.

1502
00:57:49,008 --> 00:57:51,978
I wanted to capture INGYOO's signature attitude,

1503
00:57:51,978 --> 00:57:54,288
so I decided to fill this part with different sides of his style.

1504
00:57:54,288 --> 00:57:57,188
Movements with INGYOO's own vibe.

1505
00:57:57,188 --> 00:57:58,788
About 6 or 7?

1506
00:57:58,788 --> 00:58:00,688
To improve the quality,

1507
00:58:00,688 --> 00:58:03,258
I tried creating a lot of movements.

1508
00:58:03,458 --> 00:58:05,458
Here comes INGYOO!

1509
00:58:06,058 --> 00:58:09,298
(With the group choreography ready, dancer INGYOO arrives.)

1510
00:58:09,498 --> 00:58:10,538
Seven, go!

1511
00:58:10,538 --> 00:58:11,998
(BADA's part rehearsal begins with INGYOO.)

1512
00:58:12,198 --> 00:58:15,038
(An intense gaze)

1513
00:58:15,938 --> 00:58:17,808
Just like a real villain.

1514
00:58:18,938 --> 00:58:21,148
(The villain appears.)

1515
00:58:21,148 --> 00:58:22,208
That looks cool.

1516
00:58:22,248 --> 00:58:23,608
Honestly, I wasn't sure.

1517
00:58:23,608 --> 00:58:25,718
I felt BADA had eliminated as many variables as possible.

1518
00:58:25,718 --> 00:58:26,818
Simple moves...

1519
00:58:26,818 --> 00:58:28,348
that were easy to synchronize.

1520
00:58:28,348 --> 00:58:29,888
It wasn't fun to watch.

1521
00:58:30,488 --> 00:58:31,888
Looking at just the movements,

1522
00:58:31,888 --> 00:58:33,388
I felt something was missing.

1523
00:58:33,388 --> 00:58:34,758
This is movement directing.

1524
00:58:34,758 --> 00:58:36,228
You have to radiate energy.

1525
00:58:36,328 --> 00:58:37,528
- Am I doing this? - Yes.

1526
00:58:37,798 --> 00:58:39,058
I'll show them how it's done.

1527
00:58:39,058 --> 00:58:40,368
This is movement directing.

1528
00:58:40,368 --> 00:58:41,828
I can't bring out her best in a predictable way.

1529
00:58:41,828 --> 00:58:44,738
My part doesn't have any special effects,

1530
00:58:44,738 --> 00:58:46,198
or a lot of dancers.

1531
00:58:46,198 --> 00:58:49,208
She has to do something all alone in a hallway,

1532
00:58:49,208 --> 00:58:50,268
so energy is key.

1533
00:58:50,268 --> 00:58:51,438
(An energetic forward roll?)

1534
00:58:51,438 --> 00:58:52,578
It'll look like this. Like this.

1535
00:58:52,578 --> 00:58:53,608
Then...

1536
00:58:53,608 --> 00:58:55,178
you'll turn like this as you roll.

1537
00:58:55,178 --> 00:58:56,308
A breakfall and a forward roll?

1538
00:58:56,308 --> 00:58:57,648
Out of nowhere in this part?

1539
00:58:58,078 --> 00:59:00,448
(Straight into a roll)

1540
00:59:00,448 --> 00:59:01,688
Dynamic action.

1541
00:59:01,688 --> 00:59:03,958
Powerful and energetic like that.

1542
00:59:03,958 --> 00:59:05,488
There are three eyeholes,

1543
00:59:05,488 --> 00:59:08,628
so I wanted to show three different versions of BADA.

1544
00:59:08,628 --> 00:59:11,658
One BADA focusing on sharp accents,

1545
00:59:11,658 --> 00:59:14,568
one with long reaches and big, sweeping movements,

1546
00:59:14,568 --> 00:59:17,168
and one focusing on facial expressions.

1547
00:59:17,168 --> 00:59:19,638
BADA is such a strong dancer,

1548
00:59:19,638 --> 00:59:22,308
and she's shown that so many times.

1549
00:59:22,308 --> 00:59:24,138
I thought, no dancing. None at all.

1550
00:59:24,138 --> 00:59:27,378
Why not show another side of her besides dancing?

1551
00:59:27,908 --> 00:59:29,978
(BADA is made to roll throughout rehearsal.)

1552
00:59:29,978 --> 00:59:31,548
That's it. Yes!

1553
00:59:31,548 --> 00:59:32,978
(BADA is made to roll throughout rehearsal.)

1554
00:59:32,978 --> 00:59:35,188
Nice! That was good.

1555
00:59:35,188 --> 00:59:37,288
This is how he's going to use me?

1556
00:59:37,288 --> 00:59:38,558
I wondered why.

1557
00:59:38,558 --> 00:59:40,288
What I really love...

1558
00:59:40,288 --> 00:59:41,958
is using my hair when I dance.

1559
00:59:41,958 --> 00:59:45,458
I love being in control of even my hair,

1560
00:59:45,458 --> 00:59:46,728
but after I roll,

1561
00:59:46,728 --> 00:59:48,828
my hair naturally falls in front of my face.

1562
00:59:49,398 --> 00:59:50,968
Nice!

1563
00:59:52,538 --> 00:59:53,838
But INGYOO doesn't know that.

1564
00:59:53,838 --> 00:59:55,538
He hadn't really studied me.

1565
00:59:55,538 --> 00:59:57,908
As long as the roll looks clean,

1566
00:59:57,908 --> 00:59:59,338
there's no risk in this part.

1567
00:59:59,538 --> 01:00:02,108
I felt like the roll was the only thing he'd planned.

1568
01:00:02,108 --> 01:00:04,118
For INGYOO,

1569
01:00:04,118 --> 01:00:06,918
I'd prepared 7 or 8 different movements.

1570
01:00:06,918 --> 01:00:09,548
But he'd only prepared one.

1571
01:00:09,548 --> 01:00:11,188
Honestly, even for the freestyle,

1572
01:00:11,188 --> 01:00:12,658
I thought he'd choreograph it.

1573
01:00:12,688 --> 01:00:14,188
The freestyle is separate,

1574
01:00:14,188 --> 01:00:15,528
and I'd like another one on its own.

1575
01:00:15,558 --> 01:00:17,428
But he left it entirely up to me.

1576
01:00:17,498 --> 01:00:19,358
A director has to trust the dancer.

1577
01:00:19,458 --> 01:00:22,298
(Part Movement Cross Directing: Back Koo Young & Kasper)

1578
01:00:22,528 --> 01:00:23,798
Arrived earlier.

1579
01:00:25,298 --> 01:00:27,168
Tae Woo, how's your prep for Last Stage going?

1580
01:00:27,168 --> 01:00:28,768
I'm definitely not going.

1581
01:00:30,138 --> 01:00:32,108
The situation got interesting.

1582
01:00:32,238 --> 01:00:33,778
We've never had this before, right?

1583
01:00:33,778 --> 01:00:35,648
Directing each other like this?

1584
01:00:35,648 --> 01:00:37,548
But what if the dancer gets all the moves wrong on set?

1585
01:00:37,678 --> 01:00:39,548
But we're not being judged on our dancing anyway.

1586
01:00:39,548 --> 01:00:40,588
- That's true. - You're right.

1587
01:00:40,588 --> 01:00:41,648
That'll add some tension.

1588
01:00:41,648 --> 01:00:43,388
I felt I had to keep him in check.

1589
01:00:43,488 --> 01:00:46,558
As it happens, in Koo Young's part,

1590
01:00:46,558 --> 01:00:47,728
I'm the dancer,

1591
01:00:47,858 --> 01:00:49,558
and in the part I direct,

1592
01:00:49,558 --> 01:00:52,628
Koo Young has to be the dancer.

1593
01:00:52,728 --> 01:00:54,998
I had a lot to think about.

1594
01:00:54,998 --> 01:00:57,938
My part is the fourth and final one,

1595
01:00:57,938 --> 01:01:01,808
with movements that form an endless loop.

1596
01:01:01,808 --> 01:01:05,308
I felt it needed a dreamy quality.

1597
01:01:05,378 --> 01:01:06,538
For this particular part,

1598
01:01:06,538 --> 01:01:08,148
I think taller dancers would be a good fit.

1599
01:01:08,208 --> 01:01:10,108
I thought BADA would be good,

1600
01:01:10,208 --> 01:01:11,818
but INGYOO and Koo Young...

1601
01:01:11,818 --> 01:01:13,048
(Well...)

1602
01:01:13,148 --> 01:01:14,348
It had me a little worried.

1603
01:01:14,348 --> 01:01:16,288
It didn't feel like a good fit for the song.

1604
01:01:16,288 --> 01:01:18,088
(Kasper's movement directing rehearsal begins.)

1605
01:01:18,188 --> 01:01:19,318
Set and go.

1606
01:01:21,528 --> 01:01:22,728
Oh!

1607
01:01:23,328 --> 01:01:25,028
It was better than I expected.

1608
01:01:25,028 --> 01:01:26,858
He's fluid yet powerful,

1609
01:01:26,958 --> 01:01:29,028
and his lines are beautiful.

1610
01:01:29,398 --> 01:01:30,538
I'm very satisfied.

1611
01:01:31,068 --> 01:01:32,398
I really didn't like it.

1612
01:01:32,998 --> 01:01:35,338
Among the moves he'd prepared,

1613
01:01:35,338 --> 01:01:38,038
some were pretty predictable.

1614
01:01:38,038 --> 01:01:39,478
For example, moves like this.

1615
01:01:41,548 --> 01:01:43,708
My arms and legs are short.

1616
01:01:43,778 --> 01:01:46,418
When I do simple moves like these,

1617
01:01:46,418 --> 01:01:48,188
I'm unlikely to look cool.

1618
01:01:48,318 --> 01:01:50,718
For someone built like me or INGYOO,

1619
01:01:50,718 --> 01:01:53,488
shouldn't you prepare different moves?

1620
01:01:54,158 --> 01:01:56,058
There are walls on both sides,

1621
01:01:56,428 --> 01:01:57,698
and it's really narrow.

1622
01:01:57,698 --> 01:01:59,498
It's narrow, sort of...

1623
01:01:59,498 --> 01:02:00,768
It's a scene like this.

1624
01:02:00,768 --> 01:02:01,798
Part two...

1625
01:02:01,798 --> 01:02:04,968
has a lot of dancers in a narrow hallway...

1626
01:02:05,038 --> 01:02:08,468
creating an energetic atmosphere.

1627
01:02:08,468 --> 01:02:09,938
The key is...

1628
01:02:09,938 --> 01:02:11,638
Kasper himself, really.

1629
01:02:12,108 --> 01:02:15,148
He breaks away from the dancers to create contrast,

1630
01:02:15,378 --> 01:02:16,848
drawing the focus to him.

1631
01:02:16,848 --> 01:02:20,018
It was a part that required speed and control.

1632
01:02:20,078 --> 01:02:21,848
As a dancer, Kim Tae Woo...

1633
01:02:21,848 --> 01:02:23,548
is nimble and quick.

1634
01:02:23,548 --> 01:02:24,918
Those fast moves.

1635
01:02:24,918 --> 01:02:27,158
His fingertips are strong, maybe because he boxes.

1636
01:02:27,158 --> 01:02:29,928
Grabbing and controlling things with his hands.

1637
01:02:29,928 --> 01:02:33,728
I should come up with ways to make Kasper stand out.

1638
01:02:33,728 --> 01:02:34,998
It was more fun than I expected.

1639
01:02:34,998 --> 01:02:36,568
Having such limited space...

1640
01:02:36,568 --> 01:02:39,038
actually made creating it more fun.

1641
01:02:39,038 --> 01:02:40,338
- Thank you! - Even at this stage,

1642
01:02:40,338 --> 01:02:41,508
I think it's turned out really well.

1643
01:02:41,508 --> 01:02:43,008
He was very satisfied.

1644
01:02:43,008 --> 01:02:44,238
I'm not sure.

1645
01:02:44,608 --> 01:02:45,738
It feels a little off.

1646
01:02:45,738 --> 01:02:48,008
It doesn't really match the music.

1647
01:02:48,078 --> 01:02:49,348
He wanted me to hang on...

1648
01:02:49,348 --> 01:02:52,678
and come down like this.

1649
01:02:52,748 --> 01:02:53,848
But I know...

1650
01:02:53,988 --> 01:02:55,218
it won't work.

1651
01:02:55,248 --> 01:02:57,118
They'll have temporary walls up,

1652
01:02:57,218 --> 01:02:58,858
not even real walls.

1653
01:02:58,858 --> 01:03:00,788
But he still wants to do it.

1654
01:03:00,788 --> 01:03:01,788
Fine.

1655
01:03:01,788 --> 01:03:03,658
I didn't have the guts to say,

1656
01:03:03,658 --> 01:03:05,358
"Bro, this doesn't work."

1657
01:03:05,358 --> 01:03:06,698
That was my little strategy.

1658
01:03:06,828 --> 01:03:08,368
Little by little,

1659
01:03:08,598 --> 01:03:10,428
I changed the moves behind Koo Young's back.

1660
01:03:10,528 --> 01:03:13,038
How I look on film matters, too.

1661
01:03:13,038 --> 01:03:14,568
It's about time for Koo Young to go.

1662
01:03:14,568 --> 01:03:16,538
The people want him at Last Stage.

1663
01:03:16,538 --> 01:03:17,978
It's Kasper's turn to go to Last Stage.

1664
01:03:17,978 --> 01:03:19,578
(Hyundai City Outlets, Dongdaemun)

1665
01:03:19,578 --> 01:03:21,108
(Time for a quick break!)

1666
01:03:21,108 --> 01:03:22,208
Amazing!

1667
01:03:22,508 --> 01:03:25,548
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War merch-filled pop-up)

1668
01:03:25,848 --> 01:03:28,448
- They turned out great. - So sleek!

1669
01:03:28,888 --> 01:03:30,548
- So many kinds of merch! - There are.

1670
01:03:30,548 --> 01:03:31,958
Such a wide variety.

1671
01:03:32,188 --> 01:03:34,088
Photo cards like these...

1672
01:03:34,488 --> 01:03:36,058
This is cute.

1673
01:03:36,588 --> 01:03:38,158
The key ring is so cute.

1674
01:03:38,158 --> 01:03:39,298
So cute.

1675
01:03:39,298 --> 01:03:40,398
Here's BABYZOO!

1676
01:03:41,098 --> 01:03:42,198
I like it.

1677
01:03:43,298 --> 01:03:45,798
- They made key rings, too. - They did.

1678
01:03:46,468 --> 01:03:47,668
BADA and BABYZOO.

1679
01:03:47,668 --> 01:03:49,068
- This pairing works so well. - This pairing.

1680
01:03:49,068 --> 01:03:50,308
This pairing is great.

1681
01:03:51,008 --> 01:03:52,478
Wait, what's this?

1682
01:03:52,478 --> 01:03:53,608
Like an ID photo,

1683
01:03:53,608 --> 01:03:55,248
you put your face in here.

1684
01:03:55,548 --> 01:03:57,648
If you want a Kasper key ring,

1685
01:03:57,648 --> 01:03:58,818
like I'm doing,

1686
01:03:58,918 --> 01:04:00,888
just make one and attach it.

1687
01:04:00,888 --> 01:04:02,948
It's like going back ten years.

1688
01:04:03,488 --> 01:04:05,118
It's like going back ten years.

1689
01:04:05,118 --> 01:04:06,458
Look at you.

1690
01:04:06,458 --> 01:04:07,858
(Kasper, the happy key ring guy)

1691
01:04:07,928 --> 01:04:09,628
Trading cards? What are these?

1692
01:04:09,628 --> 01:04:10,698
Let's pick one.

1693
01:04:10,728 --> 01:04:12,628
Try one each.

1694
01:04:12,628 --> 01:04:13,758
Let's see what you get.

1695
01:04:13,758 --> 01:04:15,998
One, two, three. Amazing!

1696
01:04:17,368 --> 01:04:18,968
(What surprised them?)

1697
01:04:18,968 --> 01:04:19,998
Amazing!

1698
01:04:19,998 --> 01:04:21,738
(BABYZOO and BADA both picked Koo Young.)

1699
01:04:21,738 --> 01:04:22,768
Next?

1700
01:04:22,768 --> 01:04:24,438
- One, two, three. - One, two, three.

1701
01:04:24,538 --> 01:04:25,578
BABYZOO.

1702
01:04:25,578 --> 01:04:27,348
- Oh, amazing! - What?

1703
01:04:27,348 --> 01:04:28,548
What?

1704
01:04:28,548 --> 01:04:29,908
(This time, they're surprised to pick their own photo cards.)

1705
01:04:29,908 --> 01:04:31,648
- What? - What?

1706
01:04:31,718 --> 01:04:32,818
That's amazing.

1707
01:04:32,818 --> 01:04:34,288
(With the uncles looking on blankly)

1708
01:04:34,518 --> 01:04:36,448
I'm getting goosebumps. Seriously.

1709
01:04:36,948 --> 01:04:38,458
Let's all take a photo together.

1710
01:04:38,558 --> 01:04:39,658
Like this.

1711
01:04:39,688 --> 01:04:41,428
One, two, three.

1712
01:04:41,728 --> 01:04:43,528
(The directors enjoyed their break.)

1713
01:04:43,658 --> 01:04:44,698
Look straight ahead.

1714
01:04:44,698 --> 01:04:45,758
One, two, three.

1715
01:04:45,758 --> 01:04:46,828
(Standing stiffly at attention)

1716
01:04:47,628 --> 01:04:48,928
That's pretty.

1717
01:04:48,968 --> 01:04:49,998
It turned out well.

1718
01:04:49,998 --> 01:04:50,998
(INGYOO, come with us next time!)

1719
01:04:51,098 --> 01:04:54,068
(Fully recharged)

1720
01:04:54,068 --> 01:04:55,838
(NOL Festival, Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

1721
01:04:55,838 --> 01:04:57,808
(A chance to see the TOP4 perform and take their dance classes)

1722
01:04:57,808 --> 01:04:58,938
(D-DAY of Brand Performance Film Mission)

1723
01:04:58,938 --> 01:05:00,038
- Hello. - Hello.

1724
01:05:00,038 --> 01:05:01,908
(Movement director BABYZOO arrives early to get ready.)

1725
01:05:01,908 --> 01:05:04,478
- Your first scene today is solo? - Yes.

1726
01:05:04,548 --> 01:05:06,148
Doesn't that put pressure on you?

1727
01:05:06,248 --> 01:05:07,718
No, I love it.

1728
01:05:07,718 --> 01:05:09,448
(Thrilled)

1729
01:05:09,518 --> 01:05:11,158
I love doing this solo.

1730
01:05:11,488 --> 01:05:12,758
(Bursts out laughing)

1731
01:05:12,888 --> 01:05:14,228
(Keeps breaking into laughter)

1732
01:05:14,228 --> 01:05:18,028
It was my first time modeling for such a big brand,

1733
01:05:18,028 --> 01:05:19,158
so I was really happy.

1734
01:05:19,158 --> 01:05:21,328
First off, I escaped Last Stage.

1735
01:05:21,468 --> 01:05:24,068
Honestly, that's the best part.

1736
01:05:24,198 --> 01:05:25,238
I'm looking forward to it.

1737
01:05:25,238 --> 01:05:26,268
(The movement director arrives on set.)

1738
01:05:26,268 --> 01:05:27,808
It's so spacious.

1739
01:05:27,868 --> 01:05:30,668
A huge cyclorama, even big enough for a mega crew.

1740
01:05:30,668 --> 01:05:32,038
(And being set up on one side...)

1741
01:05:32,838 --> 01:05:35,648
When I shoot demo videos for artists,

1742
01:05:35,648 --> 01:05:37,378
I often use my phone.

1743
01:05:37,418 --> 01:05:39,448
Compared to filming on a smartphone,

1744
01:05:39,448 --> 01:05:41,518
it feels a bit more vivid, I'd say.

1745
01:05:41,518 --> 01:05:42,948
More lifelike, too.

1746
01:05:42,948 --> 01:05:45,458
I think it'll capture the energy with more depth.

1747
01:05:45,458 --> 01:05:46,818
I'm really looking forward to it.

1748
01:05:47,458 --> 01:05:49,588
- Hello. - Hello.

1749
01:05:49,588 --> 01:05:52,458
Once we get the planned angle, we can shoot more...

1750
01:05:52,628 --> 01:05:53,728
- Freely. - In different styles.

1751
01:05:53,728 --> 01:05:55,368
Yes, great. We can capture it all.

1752
01:05:55,368 --> 01:05:56,498
All right.

1753
01:05:56,498 --> 01:05:57,838
When we shoot this part,

1754
01:05:57,838 --> 01:06:00,038
I think we should use the version with fewer counts.

1755
01:06:00,038 --> 01:06:02,538
Count, tick, tick, tick, tick, and one.

1756
01:06:02,538 --> 01:06:04,508
We need to play the version that starts on one.

1757
01:06:04,508 --> 01:06:06,778
That should let the dancers come in on one.

1758
01:06:06,778 --> 01:06:07,978
All right, let me check everyone.

1759
01:06:07,978 --> 01:06:09,848
How's the hair? Is it going well?

1760
01:06:09,848 --> 01:06:10,848
- Yes. - Yes.

1761
01:06:10,848 --> 01:06:13,448
As long as it's not too straight,

1762
01:06:13,548 --> 01:06:16,548
the curls should look better on camera.

1763
01:06:16,548 --> 01:06:18,118
A slightly matte look?

1764
01:06:18,118 --> 01:06:19,188
- Yes. - Yes.

1765
01:06:19,188 --> 01:06:21,328
Let's go for a take.

1766
01:06:21,658 --> 01:06:22,688
Are you ready?

1767
01:06:22,688 --> 01:06:23,988
Here we go.

1768
01:06:23,988 --> 01:06:25,098
Let's do this!

1769
01:06:25,098 --> 01:06:26,098
It's a solo section,

1770
01:06:26,098 --> 01:06:28,968
and it leads into a flashback,

1771
01:06:29,228 --> 01:06:31,468
so I need to express my emotions...

1772
01:06:31,468 --> 01:06:33,798
in a way that comes across on camera.

1773
01:06:34,708 --> 01:06:35,968
(Amazing!)

1774
01:06:35,968 --> 01:06:37,268
I really wanted to do well.

1775
01:06:37,308 --> 01:06:38,438
(Headbanging with all his might)

1776
01:06:38,538 --> 01:06:39,638
Cut!

1777
01:06:39,638 --> 01:06:40,808
(The satisfying sound of "Cut!")

1778
01:06:41,778 --> 01:06:43,578
I don't think I've ever...

1779
01:06:43,578 --> 01:06:47,688
been the star of anything in my life.

1780
01:06:47,748 --> 01:06:49,248
That's a bit much.

1781
01:06:49,618 --> 01:06:50,648
I think it's good.

1782
01:06:50,648 --> 01:06:52,218
(Satisfied)

1783
01:06:52,218 --> 01:06:54,058
Thinking that this was mine,

1784
01:06:54,058 --> 01:06:55,688
I felt my body...

1785
01:06:55,688 --> 01:06:57,188
bursting with energy.

1786
01:06:57,458 --> 01:06:59,358
We should be in sync if we just match our feet.

1787
01:06:59,358 --> 01:07:01,198
Let's match our feet.

1788
01:07:01,428 --> 01:07:04,128
Since this commercial ends...

1789
01:07:04,128 --> 01:07:06,538
with the mega crew and my solo,

1790
01:07:06,538 --> 01:07:07,908
I wanted to show not just my dream,

1791
01:07:07,908 --> 01:07:10,368
but the dreams of many people.

1792
01:07:10,368 --> 01:07:12,408
The stage I've dreamed of,

1793
01:07:12,408 --> 01:07:14,708
how I'd feel standing there,

1794
01:07:14,708 --> 01:07:17,618
I wanted to express that through the mega crew dancers.

1795
01:07:18,318 --> 01:07:20,018
Free, yet structured...

1796
01:07:20,018 --> 01:07:22,718
that's how I wanted the iconic movements to look.

1797
01:07:22,848 --> 01:07:24,758
Let's match where we look, too.

1798
01:07:25,358 --> 01:07:26,618
We're not doing this.

1799
01:07:26,618 --> 01:07:27,658
- Yes. - Yes.

1800
01:07:27,658 --> 01:07:29,188
None of this.

1801
01:07:29,288 --> 01:07:30,288
This isn't a rehearsal.

1802
01:07:30,288 --> 01:07:31,998
Get into the right emotional state.

1803
01:07:32,528 --> 01:07:34,368
(Pleased)

1804
01:07:34,968 --> 01:07:37,128
I never once thought it was hard.

1805
01:07:37,128 --> 01:07:39,498
I was happy, had fun, and think I did a good job.

1806
01:07:39,498 --> 01:07:40,698
That was great.

1807
01:07:40,908 --> 01:07:42,068
Cut!

1808
01:07:42,438 --> 01:07:43,538
- I'm hungry. - I'm hungry.

1809
01:07:43,538 --> 01:07:44,878
But we're shooting soon,

1810
01:07:44,878 --> 01:07:46,538
so there's no time to eat.

1811
01:07:46,538 --> 01:07:48,378
I had this earlier,

1812
01:07:48,378 --> 01:07:50,078
and it's great as a quick snack.

1813
01:07:50,078 --> 01:07:51,248
What's that?

1814
01:07:51,248 --> 01:07:52,548
Well, it's...

1815
01:07:52,548 --> 01:07:55,248
It doesn't just contain protein,

1816
01:07:55,248 --> 01:07:58,218
but a mix of whole-food ingredients.

1817
01:07:58,218 --> 01:07:59,958
When you're busy like we are now,

1818
01:07:59,988 --> 01:08:03,088
it's a great way to get a good mix of nutrients.

1819
01:08:03,088 --> 01:08:04,228
Give it a shake.

1820
01:08:04,228 --> 01:08:07,128
(Let's give it a good shake!)

1821
01:08:07,128 --> 01:08:08,268
(Shaking away!)

1822
01:08:08,268 --> 01:08:09,798
(BABYZOO is so cute getting into the "Royalty" shake.)

1823
01:08:09,798 --> 01:08:11,368
Just do it like this.

1824
01:08:11,368 --> 01:08:12,368
Or the finger flick dance?

1825
01:08:12,368 --> 01:08:13,398
- What's that? - You're good.

1826
01:08:13,398 --> 01:08:14,408
- You're good. - Do you prepare this...

1827
01:08:14,408 --> 01:08:16,308
in advance or something? Teach me too.

1828
01:08:16,408 --> 01:08:17,438
(Smiling innocently)

1829
01:08:17,438 --> 01:08:18,908
Teach me too.

1830
01:08:18,938 --> 01:08:20,738
(Kim Kasper born in 1992 is amazed by his dance.)

1831
01:08:20,738 --> 01:08:22,108
Let's try it.

1832
01:08:22,508 --> 01:08:24,278
The shake melts easily...

1833
01:08:24,278 --> 01:08:26,418
in both water and milk.

1834
01:08:26,518 --> 01:08:28,688
It's easy to have it whenever.

1835
01:08:28,848 --> 01:08:31,058
It's very mild and savory.

1836
01:08:31,058 --> 01:08:32,418
It isn't too strong.

1837
01:08:32,588 --> 01:08:34,488
It's perfect as a meal replacement.

1838
01:08:34,488 --> 01:08:36,958
I really have a lot of protein shake.

1839
01:08:37,028 --> 01:08:38,598
It has grains, vegetables, fruits,

1840
01:08:38,598 --> 01:08:41,098
and plant protein in one pack,

1841
01:08:41,098 --> 01:08:42,228
so it's really good.

1842
01:08:42,268 --> 01:08:43,898
It'll be good to have it when you're filming.

1843
01:08:43,898 --> 01:08:45,398
It's simple and nice.

1844
01:08:45,398 --> 01:08:46,698
If you're all done,

1845
01:08:46,698 --> 01:08:48,238
shall we go back to filming?

1846
01:08:48,468 --> 01:08:50,368
- Sounds good. - My stomach is full.

1847
01:08:50,368 --> 01:08:51,378
Let's do this, everyone!

1848
01:08:51,378 --> 01:08:52,478
- Let's go! - Yes!

1849
01:08:52,478 --> 01:08:54,848
- Let's go! - Let's go!

1850
01:08:55,948 --> 01:08:57,308
We'll start filming.

1851
01:08:57,948 --> 01:08:59,948
Five, six, seven, go.

1852
01:09:00,178 --> 01:09:02,048
(BADA is rehearsing with the dancers.)

1853
01:09:02,118 --> 01:09:04,318
If I get immersed in it and dance coolly,

1854
01:09:04,318 --> 01:09:05,658
the video will look nice.

1855
01:09:06,058 --> 01:09:08,258
She prepared it ambitiously, so I should do my best.

1856
01:09:08,928 --> 01:09:10,558
I hoped she'd give a direction...

1857
01:09:10,558 --> 01:09:13,128
which could express myself as much as possible.

1858
01:09:13,428 --> 01:09:14,528
Good.

1859
01:09:14,528 --> 01:09:18,238
The part I'm in charge of doesn't have intense dance moves.

1860
01:09:18,238 --> 01:09:19,468
INGYOO's attitude.

1861
01:09:20,368 --> 01:09:22,638
His gestures and attitude.

1862
01:09:22,768 --> 01:09:25,008
It's the part which can show...

1863
01:09:25,008 --> 01:09:27,478
INGYOO's style the best.

1864
01:09:27,578 --> 01:09:28,948
With more power.

1865
01:09:29,508 --> 01:09:30,748
Seven, go!

1866
01:09:31,248 --> 01:09:32,848
INGYOO's presence...

1867
01:09:32,848 --> 01:09:35,388
and his energy which dominates the space.

1868
01:09:36,248 --> 01:09:37,248
- Yes. - Okay.

1869
01:09:37,248 --> 01:09:38,388
(Satisfied)

1870
01:09:38,388 --> 01:09:40,288
I tried to bring that out of him.

1871
01:09:40,558 --> 01:09:42,858
Keeping a straight face doesn't look as nice as I thought.

1872
01:09:43,488 --> 01:09:44,928
I think this kind of vibe would be nice.

