01:29:29,778 --> 01:29:31,548
- My goodness. - The transition is nice.

2397
01:29:31,878 --> 01:29:33,418
The sense of action is great.

2398
01:29:36,488 --> 01:29:38,048
(Completely focused)

2399
01:29:38,958 --> 01:29:40,258
His facial expression is no joke.

2400
01:29:45,058 --> 01:29:46,258
Show us the finale, BABYZOO.

2401
01:29:46,258 --> 01:29:48,658
Even the facial expressions are spot-on, BABYZOO.

2402
01:29:52,338 --> 01:29:56,868
(ONE MOVES US ALL)

2403
01:29:59,278 --> 01:30:01,078
(You can watch their full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

2404
01:30:01,078 --> 01:30:03,048
Director, you went through a lot.

2405
01:30:03,248 --> 01:30:04,948
(Satisfied)

2406
01:30:04,948 --> 01:30:06,518
That was so cool.

2407
01:30:06,918 --> 01:30:09,018
I think Koo Young's part looks the coolest.

2408
01:30:09,018 --> 01:30:10,818
Was it because I was in it?

2409
01:30:11,048 --> 01:30:13,118
Thanks to BADA as a player,

2410
01:30:13,118 --> 01:30:14,988
an energetic part was formed,

2411
01:30:14,988 --> 01:30:17,788
which made me feel that I could probably advance to the finals.

2412
01:30:17,788 --> 01:30:20,928
Since I brought out a satisfying outcome,

2413
01:30:20,928 --> 01:30:23,968
I think I might be the one director...

2414
01:30:23,968 --> 01:30:27,238
saved to advance to the finals.

2415
01:30:27,238 --> 01:30:29,668
I was watching, completely mesmerized,

2416
01:30:29,668 --> 01:30:32,408
and only now does it hit me that this was shot on a smartphone.

2417
01:30:32,408 --> 01:30:33,438
That's right.

2418
01:30:33,438 --> 01:30:34,678
It turned out so well.

2419
01:30:35,138 --> 01:30:36,608
The quality is definitely good.

2420
01:30:36,608 --> 01:30:37,708
It's cool.

2421
01:30:37,708 --> 01:30:40,118
Since smartphones are compact,

2422
01:30:40,118 --> 01:30:42,748
the camera can squeeze into tight spaces.

2423
01:30:42,848 --> 01:30:46,188
The sense of speed and action plays a huge role.

2424
01:30:46,458 --> 01:30:48,688
I was so impressed right from the intro.

2425
01:30:48,688 --> 01:30:50,528
The section where BABYZOO choreographed...

2426
01:30:50,528 --> 01:30:52,228
- It's cool. - is great in itself,

2427
01:30:52,228 --> 01:30:54,158
and it delivered such a strong impact.

2428
01:30:54,428 --> 01:30:58,398
But since we have to pick just one person anyway,

2429
01:30:58,398 --> 01:31:00,238
shouldn't we examine this closely?

2430
01:31:00,238 --> 01:31:02,038
And I also want to listen closely to the process.

2431
01:31:02,038 --> 01:31:03,368
- Right. - Okay.

2432
01:31:03,368 --> 01:31:06,778
Before we select the one finalist,

2433
01:31:06,778 --> 01:31:09,308
a total of four parts are prepared,

2434
01:31:09,308 --> 01:31:12,478
and we are choosing one among them.

2435
01:31:12,478 --> 01:31:15,248
Personally, I liked Director INGYOO's section.

2436
01:31:15,248 --> 01:31:17,988
Looking at his directing ability on set,

2437
01:31:17,988 --> 01:31:20,618
I think it is a part where he pulled out a strong result.

2438
01:31:20,858 --> 01:31:22,358
Go down around there. Yes.

2439
01:31:22,358 --> 01:31:23,988
BADA is like a cheat code.

2440
01:31:23,988 --> 01:31:25,728
- Right. - Nobody can stop her.

2441
01:31:25,728 --> 01:31:28,658
I like that it has movements memorable to anyone.

2442
01:31:28,658 --> 01:31:31,698
A great player and a great director met,

2443
01:31:31,698 --> 01:31:35,038
and it feels like they drew out the character of BADA well.

2444
01:31:35,038 --> 01:31:36,268
I really liked it.

2445
01:31:36,538 --> 01:31:38,938
It doesn't look like there was a distinct idea behind it.

2446
01:31:38,938 --> 01:31:41,238
If you just told BADA to take care of it herself,

2447
01:31:41,238 --> 01:31:43,348
you'd get the exact same result.

2448
01:31:43,348 --> 01:31:47,218
Honestly, I think only I can pull it out to that level.

2449
01:31:47,218 --> 01:31:49,788
I try not to praise myself because it looks arrogant, but...

2450
01:31:49,788 --> 01:31:51,048
(As Director INGYOO demonstrates the movement,)

2451
01:31:51,048 --> 01:31:52,318
You just go like this.

2452
01:31:52,318 --> 01:31:55,088
(Dancer BADA shows off an even more powerful movement.)

2453
01:31:55,318 --> 01:31:56,828
Nice. We can do that.

2454
01:31:56,828 --> 01:31:57,958
I think it will work.

2455
01:31:57,958 --> 01:31:59,598
You lucked out with your player.

2456
01:31:59,598 --> 01:32:00,728
I'm really lucky.

2457
01:32:00,858 --> 01:32:03,098
If BADA were someone who normally did...

2458
01:32:03,098 --> 01:32:05,228
things like this and suddenly changed like that,

2459
01:32:05,228 --> 01:32:09,968
I'd go, "What? BADA has this side to her?"

2460
01:32:09,968 --> 01:32:12,108
But BADA always dances like that anyway.

2461
01:32:12,338 --> 01:32:16,248
Then how about the scene where BADA directed INGYOO?

2462
01:32:16,948 --> 01:32:19,648
Watching BADA's part, I figured my expectations were too high.

2463
01:32:19,648 --> 01:32:22,448
When I watched it live on set, INGYOO looked cool, though.

2464
01:32:22,548 --> 01:32:25,318
I wonder if it comes across a bit too flat.

2465
01:32:25,318 --> 01:32:28,018
It's a cut change that just glides past like this.

2466
01:32:28,018 --> 01:32:30,128
Shouldn't there have been more visual continuity?

2467
01:32:30,228 --> 01:32:31,888
I personally feel like...

2468
01:32:31,888 --> 01:32:34,198
the director might have gotten...

2469
01:32:34,198 --> 01:32:35,868
- the short end of the stick. - That makes sense.

2470
01:32:35,868 --> 01:32:39,068
Because she had to rely on limited angles in a confined space.

2471
01:32:39,068 --> 01:32:41,038
From the way I see it,

2472
01:32:41,038 --> 01:32:43,008
this is actually one of the most memorable scenes.

2473
01:32:43,208 --> 01:32:45,738
It goes room to room while keeping things simple,

2474
01:32:45,738 --> 01:32:47,208
and the building-up process...

2475
01:32:47,208 --> 01:32:49,148
was placed at just the right spots,

2476
01:32:49,148 --> 01:32:52,948
so I'd like to give that part high marks.

2477
01:32:53,448 --> 01:32:54,778
Let's move on to the next.

2478
01:32:54,778 --> 01:32:56,318
Director Koo Young's section.

2479
01:32:57,048 --> 01:32:58,048
Koo Young's section?

2480
01:32:58,048 --> 01:33:00,888
It didn't feel like Kasper's capabilities were brought out more,

2481
01:33:00,888 --> 01:33:01,958
which makes it a bit disappointing.

2482
01:33:01,958 --> 01:33:04,658
Regarding the movement, weaving the composition...

2483
01:33:04,658 --> 01:33:06,598
- into stepped formations... - It was fun.

2484
01:33:06,598 --> 01:33:07,728
was really interesting.

2485
01:33:07,728 --> 01:33:09,098
Sticking to the wall and pulling away.

2486
01:33:09,098 --> 01:33:10,328
- Right. - I was quite impressed.

2487
01:33:10,328 --> 01:33:12,998
I felt from start to finish that Director Back Koo Young...

2488
01:33:12,998 --> 01:33:14,198
was so seasoned.

2489
01:33:14,198 --> 01:33:16,068
When he first sent over the demo choreo,

2490
01:33:16,068 --> 01:33:17,538
- I gave him feedback. - Exactly.

2491
01:33:17,538 --> 01:33:20,508
And that was reflected 120 percent.

2492
01:33:20,508 --> 01:33:22,678
- Okay. - Cut.

2493
01:33:22,678 --> 01:33:23,678
(Okay, we got the shot.)

2494
01:33:23,678 --> 01:33:25,078
(Mic claps of high praise)

2495
01:33:25,078 --> 01:33:28,018
The visual I had pictured in my head translated very well.

2496
01:33:28,478 --> 01:33:30,418
- He has a lot of experience. - Right.

2497
01:33:30,418 --> 01:33:31,818
It doesn't feel like an all-out sprint,

2498
01:33:31,818 --> 01:33:33,118
but it's just complete.

2499
01:33:33,458 --> 01:33:36,258
But in Koo Young's case,

2500
01:33:36,258 --> 01:33:39,198
there were parts where BABYZOO intervened on set.

2501
01:33:39,298 --> 01:33:41,928
When I saw that, I thought it was risky.

2502
01:33:42,258 --> 01:33:45,198
Unlike the other sections,

2503
01:33:45,198 --> 01:33:47,838
my part involved quite a heavy amount of dancing.

2504
01:33:47,838 --> 01:33:49,338
So the more takes you do, the more exhausting it gets.

2505
01:33:49,338 --> 01:33:52,138
We had to shoot strictly within our physical limits.

2506
01:33:53,638 --> 01:33:56,748
Let us talk about the section where Director Kasper had...

2507
01:33:56,748 --> 01:33:59,218
- Back Koo Young as a player. - All right.

2508
01:33:59,218 --> 01:34:01,318
The moment I saw this part, I immediately thought this.

2509
01:34:01,318 --> 01:34:04,918
"Isn't this choreography made by Director Back Koo Young?"

2510
01:34:05,518 --> 01:34:07,318
It's probably because they know each other too well.

2511
01:34:07,618 --> 01:34:10,558
I feel that Kasper didn't make...

2512
01:34:10,558 --> 01:34:12,358
good use of the boundless space.

2513
01:34:12,358 --> 01:34:13,898
It felt like he didn't really get the concept.

2514
01:34:13,898 --> 01:34:17,268
The movement itself didn't feel so novel.

2515
01:34:17,268 --> 01:34:19,398
Or maybe a simpler layer?

2516
01:34:19,398 --> 01:34:21,068
I think it would've been better...

2517
01:34:21,068 --> 01:34:22,708
if that sense of infinity came through more clearly.

2518
01:34:22,708 --> 01:34:24,208
For the section I directed,

2519
01:34:24,208 --> 01:34:26,478
the director had an exact framework in mind.

2520
01:34:26,478 --> 01:34:28,608
So you could say my movement direction...

2521
01:34:28,608 --> 01:34:31,708
for what the director wanted was just flawless.

2522
01:34:31,708 --> 01:34:34,448
I bet the post-production on this must've been really tough.

2523
01:34:34,448 --> 01:34:35,478
It was hard.

2524
01:34:35,478 --> 01:34:37,918
But what was so cool was that...

2525
01:34:38,018 --> 01:34:40,388
how the dancer used his fingers right at the start.

2526
01:34:40,388 --> 01:34:41,618
On the storyboard,

2527
01:34:41,618 --> 01:34:43,588
I only gave the note that the hallway stretches,

2528
01:34:43,588 --> 01:34:44,588
with no other details.

2529
01:34:44,588 --> 01:34:46,528
Yet when he showed the movement on set, it was so cool.

2530
01:34:46,528 --> 01:34:47,558
The moment I saw that,

2531
01:34:47,558 --> 01:34:49,668
I thought it would be mind-blowing if the hallway stretched out there.

2532
01:34:50,068 --> 01:34:51,098
He gave you inspiration.

2533
01:34:51,098 --> 01:34:52,398
It feels like he's toying with the space,

2534
01:34:52,398 --> 01:34:53,868
since the hallway stretches out right after.

2535
01:34:53,868 --> 01:34:55,468
I really loved it.

2536
01:34:55,468 --> 01:34:58,138
Moves like that fit so well with that style of camera motion...

2537
01:34:58,138 --> 01:35:00,378
and post-production work.

2538
01:35:00,378 --> 01:35:02,878
- Exactly. - Those moves.

2539
01:35:02,908 --> 01:35:06,318
Actually, when I saw how proactively Kasper worked,

2540
01:35:06,318 --> 01:35:09,618
even shooting test camerawork on set, I thought he was...

2541
01:35:09,618 --> 01:35:12,888
the one who left the biggest impression.

2542
01:35:13,018 --> 01:35:14,818
Actually, this piece belongs...

2543
01:35:14,818 --> 01:35:16,528
to Director Kim Hyeong Seok,

2544
01:35:16,528 --> 01:35:18,428
and if we were simply picking great dancers,

2545
01:35:18,428 --> 01:35:20,498
BABYZOO and I should be the only ones judging them.

2546
01:35:20,498 --> 01:35:21,498
As the players.

2547
01:35:21,498 --> 01:35:23,128
- Right. - But we're selecting a director.

2548
01:35:23,128 --> 01:35:25,668
- Exactly. - We need a different perspective.

2549
01:35:25,668 --> 01:35:27,098
How smoothly they utilized their skill set...

2550
01:35:27,098 --> 01:35:30,238
to realize what Director Kim envisioned.

2551
01:35:30,338 --> 01:35:32,468
I think we need to evaluate all of that comprehensively.

2552
01:35:32,468 --> 01:35:33,478
Right.

2553
01:35:34,308 --> 01:35:35,908
(It's over!)

2554
01:35:35,908 --> 01:35:37,248
It looks like it's over.

2555
01:35:37,948 --> 01:35:39,378
(BABYZOO heads to the Directors' Room...)

2556
01:35:39,378 --> 01:35:40,818
(to select the 1 director advancing to the finals.)

2557
01:35:40,878 --> 01:35:42,648
What could BABYZOO be thinking?

2558
01:35:43,618 --> 01:35:44,648
I'm anxious.

2559
01:35:44,648 --> 01:35:47,088
Three out of four are going to the Last Stage.

2560
01:35:47,088 --> 01:35:48,618
Three-quarters are going.

2561
01:35:48,858 --> 01:35:51,358
I think the odds are 50-50.

2562
01:35:51,358 --> 01:35:54,498
The results are so neck-and-neck that it must be an agonizing choice.

2563
01:35:54,498 --> 01:35:56,498
I think they would evaluate multiple aspects equally.

2564
01:35:56,498 --> 01:35:57,568
I really don't know.

2565
01:35:57,568 --> 01:35:59,698
If they considered the behind-the-scenes process,

2566
01:35:59,698 --> 01:36:01,598
I feel like I'd shine even brighter.

2567
01:36:01,598 --> 01:36:02,738
Please.

2568
01:36:03,368 --> 01:36:05,138
Please save me.

2569
01:36:05,138 --> 01:36:07,908
If I make it to the finals,

2570
01:36:07,908 --> 01:36:09,448
I will destroy the stage. Please.

2571
01:36:09,548 --> 01:36:11,778
BABYZOO, please don't send me to the Last Stage.

2572
01:36:11,778 --> 01:36:13,178
This is hard.

2573
01:36:13,178 --> 01:36:15,548
The road to the finals is so long and brutal.

2574
01:36:15,948 --> 01:36:19,048
(Time for the final decision)

2575
01:36:19,048 --> 01:36:22,118
This is driving me crazy. Hang on. I need some time.

2576
01:36:22,558 --> 01:36:25,058
I'll just close my eyes for one minute.

2577
01:36:26,458 --> 01:36:29,368
I had to pick just one person to advance to the finals,

2578
01:36:29,368 --> 01:36:30,928
so it felt really burdensome,

2579
01:36:30,928 --> 01:36:33,168
and I wrestled with it so much mentally.

2580
01:36:33,738 --> 01:36:37,668
With these three judging criteria,

2581
01:36:37,668 --> 01:36:40,538
two of them were neck-and-neck to make the finals.

2582
01:36:40,708 --> 01:36:44,408
I'm writing down the rankings now.

2583
01:36:44,508 --> 01:36:47,718
For criteria 1 and 2, the 2 are tied.

2584
01:36:47,718 --> 01:36:51,388
But on criterion three, on-set directing and adaptability,

2585
01:36:51,388 --> 01:36:53,188
Director A edges ahead.

2586
01:36:54,558 --> 01:36:57,258
Director A gets 12 points, and Director B gets 10 points.

2587
01:36:57,828 --> 01:37:00,158
Even though the perfect score is 10, Director A received 12 points.

2588
01:37:00,158 --> 01:37:02,728
So Director A advances to the finals.

2589
01:37:03,028 --> 01:37:06,198
Your next directing mission is the Final Stage.

2590
01:37:06,938 --> 01:37:09,708
(Selection complete)

2591
01:37:09,808 --> 01:37:11,038
Am I heading over right now?

2592
01:37:14,178 --> 01:37:15,378
He's out.

2593
01:37:15,778 --> 01:37:16,978
He's out.

2594
01:37:16,978 --> 01:37:18,248
Is he out to announce the results?

2595
01:37:18,648 --> 01:37:21,578
Wait. BABYZOO is holding something.

2596
01:37:22,688 --> 01:37:23,848
(BABYZOO)

2597
01:37:23,848 --> 01:37:24,888
No.

2598
01:37:25,188 --> 01:37:26,388
Where is he going?

2599
01:37:27,088 --> 01:37:28,318
(Looking away)

2600
01:37:28,618 --> 01:37:30,288
BABYZOO can't even meet my eyes.

2601
01:37:30,288 --> 01:37:31,958
(I'm going to the Last Stage?)

2602
01:37:32,158 --> 01:37:34,758
(Marching forward without locking eyes with anyone)

2603
01:37:35,758 --> 01:37:37,268
He's going over to Koo Young.

2604
01:37:37,368 --> 01:37:38,428
Is he coming to me?

2605
01:37:38,428 --> 01:37:40,168
No!

2606
01:37:40,168 --> 01:37:41,598
He's heading for Koo Young's room.

2607
01:37:41,768 --> 01:37:42,968
Is it Koo Young?

2608
01:37:45,538 --> 01:37:46,578
Come in.

2609
01:37:46,778 --> 01:37:50,048
Thank you so much for participating today.

2610
01:37:51,748 --> 01:37:53,018
- Here. - Good work today.

2611
01:37:53,018 --> 01:37:54,818
- I'll leave this right here. - Okay. Thanks.

2612
01:37:54,818 --> 01:37:55,818
(Bowing)

2613
01:37:56,918 --> 01:37:59,588
Out of nowhere, BABYZOO walked in carrying an envelope.

2614
01:38:01,188 --> 01:38:03,028
The result for the one finalist.

2615
01:38:03,658 --> 01:38:06,858
It seems like who gets to advance to the finals is in here.

2616
01:38:07,258 --> 01:38:09,368
I did get my hopes up a little.

2617
01:38:09,728 --> 01:38:10,968
Did Koo Young survive?

2618
01:38:11,168 --> 01:38:12,228
Did Koo Young survive?

2619
01:38:12,228 --> 01:38:13,838
Only Koo Young survived?

2620
01:38:14,598 --> 01:38:15,838
He must be happy.

2621
01:38:15,938 --> 01:38:17,868
So I'm going to the Last Stage.

2622
01:38:18,568 --> 01:38:19,708
(Sighing)

2623
01:38:20,138 --> 01:38:22,778
Koo Young should go to the Last Stage.

2624
01:38:23,108 --> 01:38:25,378
He needs to get dropped into that inferno too.

2625
01:38:26,178 --> 01:38:28,148
(BABYZOO is back in the Director's Room.)

2626
01:38:28,878 --> 01:38:30,918
(Preparing the next envelope)

2627
01:38:32,148 --> 01:38:34,858
Wait, there are multiple envelopes.

2628
01:38:34,888 --> 01:38:36,258
(But only one person advances to the finals.)

2629
01:38:36,258 --> 01:38:37,658
It was a bomb letter!

2630
01:38:38,028 --> 01:38:39,258
It was a bomb letter!

2631
01:38:39,358 --> 01:38:41,198
That thing is like a "Death Note".

2632
01:38:41,198 --> 01:38:42,458
(A death letter bound for the Last Stage?)

2633
01:38:42,768 --> 01:38:44,298
(Chuckling)

2634
01:38:44,428 --> 01:38:45,998
What on earth is this?

2635
01:38:46,298 --> 01:38:47,338
What?

2636
01:38:47,338 --> 01:38:48,538
Is it starting up again?

2637
01:38:48,838 --> 01:38:50,108
He's coming again.

2638
01:38:51,138 --> 01:38:52,668
BABYZOO is coming.

2639
01:38:52,908 --> 01:38:55,008
He heads into Kasper's room.

2640
01:38:55,478 --> 01:38:58,078
No way. Is this the order of going to the Last Stage?

2641
01:38:58,548 --> 01:39:00,048
Okay. As long as it isn't me.

2642
01:39:00,048 --> 01:39:01,648
It's fine as long as it's not me.

2643
01:39:01,918 --> 01:39:03,218
What's the order behind handing out these letters?

2644
01:39:03,218 --> 01:39:04,518
Right as I was thinking that...

2645
01:39:04,518 --> 01:39:05,588
(Knocking)

2646
01:39:06,488 --> 01:39:08,218
You worked so hard today.

2647
01:39:08,718 --> 01:39:10,328
He bowed 90 degrees to me.

2648
01:39:10,828 --> 01:39:12,088
Thank you for your hard work.

2649
01:39:12,828 --> 01:39:15,058
That is a condolence bow.

2650
01:39:15,658 --> 01:39:17,568
Wasn't that polite 90-degree bow...

2651
01:39:17,568 --> 01:39:18,668
