2652
01:39:19,268 --> 01:39:21,198
So this confirms it.

2653
01:39:21,198 --> 01:39:22,398
I'm going to the Last Stage.

2654
01:39:22,398 --> 01:39:23,538
I didn't make the cut.

2655
01:39:23,668 --> 01:39:25,668
This is a letter. Please open it...

2656
01:39:25,668 --> 01:39:27,878
when they give you...

2657
01:39:27,878 --> 01:39:29,778
the cue later.

2658
01:39:30,308 --> 01:39:31,478
What happens if I open it before then?

2659
01:39:31,478 --> 01:39:33,318
Then you get scolded.

2660
01:39:33,418 --> 01:39:34,478
- Thank you. - You know,

2661
01:39:34,478 --> 01:39:35,778
I'm getting ready for the Last Stage now.

2662
01:39:35,848 --> 01:39:37,688
I'm already ordering props.

2663
01:39:37,748 --> 01:39:39,558
(Avoiding his eyes)

2664
01:39:39,558 --> 01:39:40,888
Thank you for everything.

2665
01:39:42,588 --> 01:39:45,928
(BABYZOO leaves.)

2666
01:39:46,028 --> 01:39:47,498
I'm definitely going to the Last Stage.

2667
01:39:48,398 --> 01:39:51,228
I think he's only handing envelopes to the ones going to the Last Stage.

2668
01:39:51,628 --> 01:39:54,898
Look at BABYZOO's mood before handing out the final bomb letter.

2669
01:39:54,898 --> 01:39:56,708
Totally shaded in distress.

2670
01:39:56,908 --> 01:39:59,268
I really want to go home.

2671
01:39:59,738 --> 01:40:00,778
(Sighing)

2672
01:40:00,808 --> 01:40:02,278
(In agony)

2673
01:40:02,278 --> 01:40:03,378
(Groaning)

2674
01:40:04,608 --> 01:40:07,118
I hope this is the order of people going to the Last Stage.

2675
01:40:07,278 --> 01:40:08,678
Koo Young goes down first.

2676
01:40:08,678 --> 01:40:10,248
Kasper goes next.

2677
01:40:10,318 --> 01:40:11,648
And after that, it has to be INGYOO.

2678
01:40:11,648 --> 01:40:12,958
It has to be INGYOO.

2679
01:40:13,418 --> 01:40:14,558
It's me.

2680
01:40:14,558 --> 01:40:15,788
(BABYZOO)

2681
01:40:15,788 --> 01:40:17,428
He's going to BADA.

2682
01:40:17,628 --> 01:40:19,928
BADA, you did a great job.

2683
01:40:20,058 --> 01:40:22,298
- Thank you for your great work. - My pleasure.

2684
01:40:22,298 --> 01:40:23,798
- You went through a lot. - You did too.

2685
01:40:23,798 --> 01:40:25,498
This is a letter.

2686
01:40:25,498 --> 01:40:26,698
A letter?

2687
01:40:26,698 --> 01:40:27,738
Thank you.

2688
01:40:27,738 --> 01:40:28,838
- Thank you. - Thank you for your hard work.

2689
01:40:29,198 --> 01:40:30,338
(He visits INGYOO's room.)

2690
01:40:30,338 --> 01:40:31,738
Good work, INGYOO.

2691
01:40:31,738 --> 01:40:32,938
Good work.

2692
01:40:33,578 --> 01:40:37,008
You hit your absolute peak today.

2693
01:40:37,378 --> 01:40:39,148
He goes to INGYOO with a smile.

2694
01:40:39,478 --> 01:40:41,718
Does that smile mean, "Goodbye, INGYOO"?

2695
01:40:42,048 --> 01:40:43,348
- I did? - You broke through the ceiling.

2696
01:40:43,348 --> 01:40:44,418
I'm glad to hear that.

2697
01:40:44,418 --> 01:40:45,818
This is a letter.

2698
01:40:45,848 --> 01:40:47,688
- Did you write it? - Yes, I did.

2699
01:40:47,688 --> 01:40:49,118
Isn't it a bomb?

2700
01:40:49,258 --> 01:40:50,928
A bomb... Good work, BABYZOO.

2701
01:40:50,928 --> 01:40:52,328
Good work, INGYOO.

2702
01:40:53,628 --> 01:40:56,098
(They all received the letters.)

2703
01:40:56,098 --> 01:40:57,228
(BADA)

2704
01:40:57,528 --> 01:40:59,968
The result is inside this envelope.

2705
01:41:00,198 --> 01:41:01,298
What could it be?

2706
01:41:01,768 --> 01:41:03,208
Shall we open the gift?

2707
01:41:03,838 --> 01:41:05,968
(Announcing the one Director advancing to the Finals)

2708
01:41:05,968 --> 01:41:07,808
(Surprised)

2709
01:41:07,808 --> 01:41:08,838
Can I open it?

2710
01:41:08,838 --> 01:41:09,948
It's finally announced?

2711
01:41:10,348 --> 01:41:11,678
What do I do?

2712
01:41:12,078 --> 01:41:13,948
(I'll hide for a moment.)

2713
01:41:15,048 --> 01:41:16,488
(Sighing)

2714
01:41:17,688 --> 01:41:20,418
(Without going to the Last Stage,)

2715
01:41:21,518 --> 01:41:24,158
(which director will head straight to the finals?)

2716
01:41:26,428 --> 01:41:28,558
(Announcing the one Director advancing to the Finals)

2717
01:41:28,698 --> 01:41:30,198
(Surprised)

2718
01:41:31,198 --> 01:41:32,668
(Sighing)

2719
01:41:33,438 --> 01:41:36,608
(Without going to the Last Stage,)

2720
01:41:37,868 --> 01:41:39,778
(which director will head straight to the finals?)

2721
01:41:41,678 --> 01:41:44,148
Director INGYOO, your next directing mission...

2722
01:41:44,148 --> 01:41:46,518
is Last Stage: 24H.

2723
01:41:46,548 --> 01:41:48,348
(Chuckling)

2724
01:41:48,548 --> 01:41:50,148
Last Stage does feel like...

2725
01:41:50,248 --> 01:41:51,618
my personal color, honestly.

2726
01:41:51,948 --> 01:41:53,888
(Accepting the result)

2727
01:41:54,118 --> 01:41:55,488
(Back Koo Young checks his result.)

2728
01:41:55,488 --> 01:41:56,928
(Reading carefully)

2729
01:41:56,928 --> 01:41:58,128
(Exclaiming)

2730
01:41:58,158 --> 01:42:00,758
"Your next directing mission is Last Stage: 24H."

2731
01:42:00,758 --> 01:42:02,328
Gosh, seriously...

2732
01:42:02,398 --> 01:42:03,598
I didn't see this coming.

2733
01:42:04,328 --> 01:42:06,228
The dancers' details weren't...

2734
01:42:06,228 --> 01:42:08,198
aligned on set during filming.

2735
01:42:08,598 --> 01:42:11,068
Do all the dancers bow their heads on this movement?

2736
01:42:11,068 --> 01:42:12,308
- No. - They shouldn't, right?

2737
01:42:12,368 --> 01:42:13,538
When you do this...

2738
01:42:13,538 --> 01:42:16,778
I stepped in to sort out the details with the dancers.

2739
01:42:16,778 --> 01:42:17,948
(BABYZOO sorted out the fine details that Back Koo Young missed.)

2740
01:42:18,178 --> 01:42:19,878
My eyes were already caught...

2741
01:42:19,878 --> 01:42:21,348
on the dancers' lack of detail,

2742
01:42:21,348 --> 01:42:23,418
which made it quite disappointing.

2743
01:42:23,648 --> 01:42:25,348
For INGYOO,

2744
01:42:25,388 --> 01:42:26,888
BADA performed so remarkably...

2745
01:42:27,218 --> 01:42:28,418
that his ratings are high.

2746
01:42:28,558 --> 01:42:30,658
But the actual shooting process was slightly less seamless...

2747
01:42:30,658 --> 01:42:33,928
compared to the other Part Movement Directors.

2748
01:42:34,258 --> 01:42:35,858
How do we bring that to life?

2749
01:42:36,258 --> 01:42:37,368
Like this.

2750
01:42:37,368 --> 01:42:41,168
(BADA was busy dealing with the impromptu directing.)

2751
01:42:41,438 --> 01:42:43,168
You lucked out with your player.

2752
01:42:43,238 --> 01:42:44,308
I'm really lucky.

2753
01:42:44,938 --> 01:42:46,938
(Only 2 directors remain.)

2754
01:42:47,108 --> 01:42:49,108
I might be the one director...

2755
01:42:49,108 --> 01:42:52,378
saved to advance to the finals.

2756
01:42:52,508 --> 01:42:54,378
I submitted the textbook answer...

2757
01:42:54,378 --> 01:42:56,388
that aligned perfectly with the evaluation criteria.

2758
01:42:57,818 --> 01:42:59,088
(Surprised)

2759
01:42:59,088 --> 01:43:01,558
(Your next directing mission is the Final Stage.)

2760
01:43:01,988 --> 01:43:03,058
(Kasper advances to the finals.)

2761
01:43:03,058 --> 01:43:04,228
(Director advancing to the Final Stage: Kasper)

2762
01:43:05,028 --> 01:43:06,598
(Muted celebration)

2763
01:43:07,858 --> 01:43:09,458
I can't believe this.

2764
01:43:10,028 --> 01:43:11,868
I have to take a photo of this.

2765
01:43:12,098 --> 01:43:13,338
It's finally happening.

2766
01:43:13,398 --> 01:43:15,038
I made it to the finals.

2767
01:43:15,368 --> 01:43:17,038
I'm so happy.

2768
01:43:17,068 --> 01:43:19,408
I won't have to go to the Last Stage again.

2769
01:43:19,908 --> 01:43:21,508
I'm going to the Last Stage.

2770
01:43:21,508 --> 01:43:22,578
(BADA's next directing mission: Last Stage: 24H)

2771
01:43:22,578 --> 01:43:23,848
(Your next directing mission is Last Stage: 24H.)

2772
01:43:24,248 --> 01:43:26,048
I'm quite shocked.

2773
01:43:26,148 --> 01:43:28,448
It feels like torture with false hope.

2774
01:43:29,348 --> 01:43:33,558
"There was someone who showed a slightly better performance."

2775
01:43:33,858 --> 01:43:35,018
Who is it?

2776
01:43:35,958 --> 01:43:38,628
If it were you, Director Kim,

2777
01:43:38,988 --> 01:43:41,758
which director's section would have taken first place?

2778
01:43:41,758 --> 01:43:43,098
What we are choosing...

2779
01:43:43,098 --> 01:43:44,898
- is a director, not a player. - Right.

2780
01:43:44,898 --> 01:43:46,768
A good director needs to communicate well,

2781
01:43:46,768 --> 01:43:47,968
persuade effectively,

2782
01:43:47,968 --> 01:43:49,198
and lead the flow smoothly.

2783
01:43:49,198 --> 01:43:52,738
It demands multiple qualities.

2784
01:43:52,838 --> 01:43:54,178
From that angle,

2785
01:43:54,178 --> 01:43:55,608
my choice narrows down...

2786
01:43:55,608 --> 01:43:58,448
to BADA and Kasper.

2787
01:43:58,578 --> 01:44:00,648
BADA is a full 100 out of 100 points.

2788
01:44:00,648 --> 01:44:02,048
She was perfect.

2789
01:44:02,048 --> 01:44:03,248
"She's the one."

2790
01:44:03,248 --> 01:44:05,648
That's how I felt.

2791
01:44:05,648 --> 01:44:07,588
Then Kasper suddenly showed up.

2792
01:44:07,618 --> 01:44:11,228
Taking part in directing so exceptionally.

2793
01:44:11,328 --> 01:44:12,588
When I watched him work,

2794
01:44:12,588 --> 01:44:14,728
it served as a huge inspiration on set.

2795
01:44:14,728 --> 01:44:16,428
Kasper is also a 100 out of 100,

2796
01:44:16,498 --> 01:44:18,868
but I think he smashed right through the ceiling.

2797
01:44:18,968 --> 01:44:21,098
That is pretty much how I felt.

2798
01:44:21,098 --> 01:44:22,138
I think you felt the exact same way I did.

2799
01:44:22,138 --> 01:44:24,068
Overall, that was my exact impression.

2800
01:44:24,538 --> 01:44:26,208
Thank you, Main Movement Director.

2801
01:44:26,208 --> 01:44:27,338
Congratulations.

2802
01:44:27,338 --> 01:44:29,038
Thanks to you, I have set foot...

2803
01:44:29,038 --> 01:44:30,448
- in the finals. - My pleasure.

2804
01:44:30,508 --> 01:44:32,048
Let us show them what we've got in the finals.

2805
01:44:32,048 --> 01:44:33,118
We're the new faces.

2806
01:44:33,118 --> 01:44:34,478
The two new faces.

2807
01:44:36,548 --> 01:44:39,248
Among the three choreographers heading to the Last Stage,

2808
01:44:39,248 --> 01:44:41,118
only one will be...

2809
01:44:41,388 --> 01:44:42,518
eliminated.

2810
01:44:48,858 --> 01:44:50,768
(Laughing hysterically)

2811
01:44:51,628 --> 01:44:53,898
The reason I joined this show...

2812
01:44:53,998 --> 01:44:56,398
Four years ago, I landed in the elimination battle...

2813
01:44:56,398 --> 01:44:57,808
and lost in the semifinals,

2814
01:44:57,808 --> 01:44:59,608
missing out on the finals.

2815
01:44:59,608 --> 01:45:00,738
That's why I came on this show.

2816
01:45:00,738 --> 01:45:02,108
I can't repeat...

2817
01:45:02,338 --> 01:45:04,178
the same mistake again.

2818
01:45:04,578 --> 01:45:07,518
Now that I'm going to the Last Stage,

2819
01:45:07,618 --> 01:45:08,878
my time has come.

2820
01:45:09,048 --> 01:45:10,248
You'll see the best piece ever.

2821
01:45:10,348 --> 01:45:12,188
I will pour everything out...

2822
01:45:12,218 --> 01:45:13,458
to become the director...

2823
01:45:13,458 --> 01:45:14,788
who snatches the ticket to the finals.

2824
01:45:14,788 --> 01:45:16,058
(Who will be the director to return from Last Stage: 24H...)

2825
01:45:16,058 --> 01:45:17,388
(and advance to the finals?)

2826
01:45:17,688 --> 01:45:22,398
(Brand Performance Film Mission)

2827
01:45:22,398 --> 01:45:26,128
(This film was shot on a smartphone.)

2828
01:46:08,608 --> 01:46:11,708
(Additional equipment and software were used.)

2829
01:49:04,888 --> 01:49:07,188
(Smirking creepily)

2830
01:49:07,188 --> 01:49:09,688
(Grinning)

2831
01:49:09,688 --> 01:49:11,258
(This is a weird feeling.)

2832
01:49:11,258 --> 01:49:12,828
(I'm just one step away from the finals.)

2833
01:49:13,058 --> 01:49:15,028
(It's going to be do or die.)

2834
01:49:15,028 --> 01:49:16,928
(I can't do this.)

2835
01:49:19,068 --> 01:49:20,398
(Sighing)

2836
01:49:20,698 --> 01:49:23,508
(Hugging)

2837
01:49:23,508 --> 01:49:24,808
(You can do this.)

2838
01:49:24,808 --> 01:49:28,178
(I keep having these close calls.)

2839
01:49:28,178 --> 01:49:29,178
(Is it driving you crazy?)

2840
01:49:29,178 --> 01:49:30,548
(I just want...)

2841
01:49:30,548 --> 01:49:31,608
(to let things go now.)

2842
01:49:31,608 --> 01:49:33,978
(We're going to be super strong after this.)

2843
01:49:33,978 --> 01:49:35,848
(I don't know. I just want to make sure...)

2844
01:49:35,848 --> 01:49:37,048
(I have no regrets with Last Stage.)

2845
01:49:37,048 --> 01:49:38,818
(We must crush it if we can. That's our only choice.)

2846
01:49:38,818 --> 01:49:39,988
(We must crush it if we can. That's our only choice.)

2847
01:49:39,988 --> 01:49:42,088
(I feel bad for INGYOO and BADA.)

2848
01:49:42,088 --> 01:49:43,188
(I'm going to...)

2849
01:49:43,188 --> 01:49:46,028
(put on a performance that will guarantee my spot in the finals.)

2850
01:49:46,128 --> 01:49:47,128
(A sharp inhale)

2851
01:49:47,128 --> 01:49:48,658
(I need to make it look good.)

2852
01:49:48,658 --> 01:49:51,198
(The last object of Last Stage is...)

2853
01:49:51,198 --> 01:49:52,198
(It's...)

2854
01:49:52,198 --> 01:49:53,198
(color.)

2855
01:49:53,198 --> 01:49:54,398
(Last Stage: 24H)

2856
01:49:54,398 --> 01:49:57,038
(You've been given a unique color from the start of the competition.)

2857
01:49:57,238 --> 01:49:58,808
(You must showcase...)

2858
01:49:58,808 --> 01:50:00,378
(your unique directing style you built on your own...)

2859
01:50:00,578 --> 01:50:02,878
(and your designated color in one performance.)

2860
01:50:02,878 --> 01:50:04,908
(When I thought about the color, purple...)

2861
01:50:05,278 --> 01:50:06,848
(Back Koo Young's concept: Bruise)

2862
01:50:06,848 --> 01:50:08,148
(I wanted to convey the color...)

2863
01:50:08,148 --> 01:50:10,448
(with the techniques that matched my concept.)

2864
01:50:10,448 --> 01:50:12,118
(I can't have it any other way.)

2865
01:50:12,118 --> 01:50:13,118
(I must go to the finals.)

2866
01:50:13,118 --> 01:50:14,588
(BADA equals sky blue.)

2867
01:50:14,588 --> 01:50:16,758
(The secret weapon of my performance is me.)

2868
01:50:16,758 --> 01:50:20,058
(I'm a director who's only one step away from the finals.)

2869
01:50:20,058 --> 01:50:23,058
(I'm going to showcase all of my dancing styles on this stage.)

2870
01:50:23,058 --> 01:50:24,468
(So I'm going to survive this.)

2871
01:50:24,468 --> 01:50:26,528
(I wasn't too thrilled about green that seen.)

2872
01:50:26,528 --> 01:50:28,098
(With good energy and good art,)

2873
01:50:28,098 --> 01:50:30,168
(I'm going to paint my world green.)

2874
01:50:30,168 --> 01:50:31,408
(I'll stick to my style a little more.)

2875
01:50:31,408 --> 01:50:33,338
(This performance is the ultimate compilation...)

2876
01:50:33,338 --> 01:50:35,278
(of everything I do best.)

2877
01:50:35,508 --> 01:50:37,608
(I do think that I have a shot.)

2878
01:50:37,608 --> 01:50:40,648
(The very last episode of Last Stage: 24H...)

2879
01:50:40,648 --> 01:50:41,648
(begins now.)

2880
01:50:41,648 --> 01:50:43,078
(Nervous)

2881
01:50:43,078 --> 01:50:44,888
(I'm nervous to watch it.)

2882
01:50:47,218 --> 01:50:48,658
(Gosh, BADA is so cool.)

2883
01:50:48,658 --> 01:50:49,818
(She should do more of that.)

2884
01:50:50,858 --> 01:50:52,658
(It was close to perfection.)

2885
01:50:53,058 --> 01:50:54,698
(Back Koo Young is definitely making himself useful.)

2886
01:50:54,698 --> 01:50:55,698
(Are we in the finals already?)

2887
01:50:56,058 --> 01:50:57,068
(This is it!)

2888
01:50:57,068 --> 01:50:58,368
(This is what I'm talking about.)

2889
01:50:58,428 --> 01:51:00,768
(Amazing!)

2890
01:51:01,168 --> 01:51:02,498
